('06d83802-b910-43df-920e-540dadc358bd', 'The Players Fund', 'venture_capital', 'venture_capital', 'organization', 'Athlete-led venture capital for early-stage founders.', 'The Players Fund is a London-based venture capital firm, distinguished as the UK''s first to be led by athletes. Launched in August 2023, the firm was founded to empower the athlete community as investors and leverage their unique influence to support entrepreneurs. The fund was established through the consolidation of several athlete-founded collectives, including 4CAST, ForGood, and B-Engaged. This merger created a unified platform bringing together influential athlete investors with seasoned venture capitalists. The firm is managed by co-founding partners Fergus and Ruari Bell. Fergus, a former professional athlete, and Ruari, a consumer expert and Forbes 30 Under 30 honoree, previously co-founded 4CAST, an athlete entrepreneurial collective, which laid the groundwork for The Players Fund. The founding athlete partners include prominent figures from cricket and football, such as Ben Stokes, Jos Buttler, KL Rahul, Chris Smalling, Héctor Bellerín, and Serge Gnabry, who have ownership in the fund and provide operational input. The Players Fund operates with a £40 million fund, targeting investments in early-stage companies from pre-seed to Series A. Its business model is centered on co-investing alongside other venture capital firms rather than leading investment rounds. The firm writes initial checks ranging from £50,000 to £300,000. The investment strategy focuses on tech-enabled startups, particularly in sectors like B2B software, SaaS, health tech, fintech, AI, media, and…', 'https://playersfund.vc', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/players-fund/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2024/04/09/2ed85359636bebc6b11f4350f0d529d2.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/investors/the_players_fund', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, null, null, 'GBP', 'SEED', 'SEED|Other|Seed|Series A', 'Other:1|Seed:1|Series A:1', null, '2025-10', 7, 3),
