('f76c1ca7-944b-4037-9c13-1af0750469ca', 'Frontier Computing', 'Scalable biological brains for ML training substrates.', 'Frontier Computing, founded in 2025 by Michael Domarkas and backed by Y Combinator, operates at the intersection of biotechnology and artificial intelligence. The company is developing scalable biological neural networks to serve as a substrate for machine learning training, addressing the high costs associated with training large parameter count models on traditional hardware. The core of Frontier''s offering is a proprietary tissue-culture approach that overcomes the traditional limitations of in-vitro neuron scaling. While academic efforts have generally been confined to approximately 1 million neurons, Frontier has engineered a method to surpass this, with a pathway to scale to over 100 million neurons. This is achieved by solving the vascularization problem, which limits oxygen supply to cells in larger cultures. This technology collocates memory and compute at the substrate level, which enables the training of models with significantly larger parameter counts than what is tractable with conventional GPU architectures. Founder Michael Domarkas, a former Cambridge Natural Scientist, began culturing neuronal tissues with grant funding at the age of 17. His work led to the development of a scalable neuronal culture platform, which he validated by training a biological brain to play the game ''Frogger''. Frontier Computing is now focused on growing exascale biocomputing clusters. The company aims to launch a 500 million biological neuron cluster by January 2027. The company''s …', 'https://frontier.site', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/frontier-computing-corp/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/d579f0e592c8562cdd12098dcf802e89.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/frontier_computing', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Hardware|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Health|AI Chips and Processors|DT and LS|YC S26|science-based|Semiconductors', '2025', '3', 7670451, 'life_sciences'),
('e79da085-fdbd-4727-b100-27b8463eb116', 'Klaris', 'AI-powered platform automating MedTech regulatory compliance', 'Klaris.ai is a London-based company founded in 2024 by Francesco Corazza and Mihai Sorin that provides an artificial intelligence-powered platform to automate regulatory compliance for the medical technology industry. The firm targets MedTech SMEs, aiming to reduce the significant time and resources these companies spend on compliance-related tasks. It is backed by investors including Antler, Vento, and Alecla7. The company''s core service streamlines the creation and management of regulatory documentation required for medical devices. The platform features an AI auditor that performs instant gap analysis on technical dossiers, cross-document consistency checks, and identifies what is missing or incorrect with high accuracy. It provides actionable remediation guidance with regulatory citations to help users fix issues quickly and ensure documentation is audit-ready and compliant with standards like the Medical Device Regulation (MDR). This automation allows R&D teams to focus on developing new products rather than on administrative compliance work, aiming to accelerate the time-to-market for medical innovations. Klaris states its MVP achieved a 99% reduction in GAP analysis time for a design partner, cutting the process from one week to one hour. The business model appears to be subscription-based, offering various plans for different team sizes, including a free trial. The platform is designed to integrate with existing client workflows and ensures enterprise-grade security,…', 'https://klaris.ai', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/klaris-ai/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/03/24/cd5a695bb9241a8bb767e921fbc4d9dd.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/klaris_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Legal Documents Management|RegTech & Compliance|Health|Legal|Core AI|Medical Data|Governance, Risk and Compliance|AI Applications', '2024', '6', 1036666, 'life_sciences'),
('56774633-cb34-440e-958b-72bc6a788012', 'XARlabs', 'Device-agnostic real-time AI for the operating room', 'XRlabs is a London, UK-based company providing a surgical intelligence platform that embeds real-time AI into the operating room. Its modular, device-agnostic software runs as an external AI layer across existing surgical systems, using computer vision and deep learning to turn live surgical video into real-time intelligence at the point of care. The platform fuses live surgical video, navigation telemetry and pre-operative CT and MRI imaging into a single real-time, anatomy-aware view of the operation, and integrates with hardware hospitals already own, such as 4K 3D surgical scopes and navigation systems. The company works with partner institutions on three continents and is led by founder and CEO Dr. Ali Haddad. In October 2026, XRlabs raised $8.4 million in seed funding led by Playground Global with participation from Eka Ventures, complemented by a compute allocation from the UK Government on the UK AI Research Resource, to grow its engineering and clinical teams, advance the platform through regulatory pathways in the UK, Europe and the United States and expand its clinical evidence base. Sources: xrlabs.ai; FinSMEs (20 October 2026).', 'https://xrlabs.ai', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/xrlabs-ai/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/fc4ec5e1759699c5add983cce0d9d2cc.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/xarlabs', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.51485, -0.1256788, 'Life sciences|3D Technology|Medical Devices|Health|Surgery|Medical Education|Immersive Technologies|uk is8 life sciences', '2024', '13', 8106057, 'life_sciences'),
('8b754aaa-d242-4a22-a9ee-eec7466c724f', 'Emerald', 'GP-backed preventive Health OS combining blood tests, wearables and AI', 'Emerald is a UK preventive-health platform founded in 2024 by Alexander Badalyan (CEO) with CMO Dr Daniel McNally (active NHS clinician). It unifies baseline blood testing (115+ biomarkers across 50+ UK locations), wearable and lifestyle data, AI alerts and an assigned GP who can diagnose, prescribe and issue personalised action plans — aiming to move care from reactive GP visits to ongoing prevention under CQC registration. The company launched from stealth with £625,000 in angel funding (May 2025 coverage) and in January 2026 closed a further $1.2 million pre-seed led by Boost Capital Partners, with Mark Fountain, Granatus Ventures and angels including Premier League players, taking disclosed total to about $2 million alongside an Innovate UK grant. Traction cited includes tens of thousands of tests processed and strong NPS as the user base scaled after beta expansion. Proceeds fund UK growth, coaching programmes and lab/imaging partnerships. Sources: Tech Funding News 29 Jan 2026; Soapbox / TFN £625k launch coverage.', 'https://withemerald.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/emerald-health/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/25/709ccdbfda01fc09ab96211f6f516498.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/emerald_5', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Biomarkers|Health Diagnostics|Tech for Patients|Preventive Care|out of stealth', '2024', '25', 2992236, 'life_sciences'),
('b43407fd-3232-4f59-b158-84f814c5902e', 'neubond', 'Wearable rehabilitation devices for at-home stroke recovery', 'Neubond, a London-based therapeutic device company founded in 2024, is focused on the neurorehabilitation market, specifically targeting mobility recovery for stroke patients. The company emerged as a spin-off from Imperial College London, born from a project in the Department of Bioengineering. Its establishment was driven by co-founders Dr. Patrick Sagastegui and Jumpei Kashiwakura. Their collaboration began while developing a prosthetic hand, during which they identified a significant opportunity in the sensor interface that detects the user''s intention to move. Dr. Sagastegui, a bioengineer with a PhD in neuromodulation and over nine years of experience in electronics design, and Mr. Kashiwakura, a mechanical and bioengineer with a background as a system engineer at Toyota Motor Corp, both possess more than six years of experience in neurological rehabilitation. This shared expertise in prosthetics and assistive technology revealed a gap in post-stroke recovery solutions, inspiring them to pivot and create Neubond. The company''s core product is a wearable home rehabilitation device designed to be discreet, lightweight, and integrated into a patient''s daily life. This device utilizes a technology called volitional-induced paired associative stimulation (VIPAS). It operates as a closed-loop system where a high-density grid of miniaturized sensors detects the subtle electrical signals from the brain indicating an intention to move a limb. At that precise moment, the device …', 'https://neubond.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/neubond/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/09/408e851bc2da7a23b8d7fd8eb6255b1d.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/neubond', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Rehabilitation|Health|Neurology|Neuromodulation and Neurostimulation|Spinout|Wearable|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based|stroke', '2024', '16', 2524575, 'life_sciences'),
('a6c1da43-e985-4fdf-a139-2202793ae072', 'Fraiya', 'AI enabled pregnancy ultrasound', 'Fraiya Ltd, established in London in 2023, is a spin-out from King''s College London and Guy''s and St Thomas'' NHS Foundation Trust. The company was co-founded by Alfonso Farruggia and Sam Budd to commercialize research from the iFind (intelligent Fetal Imaging and Diagnosis) project. The founding team is a blend of clinicians, engineers, and scientists, with Professor Reza Razavi, a clinician scientist and pediatric cardiologist, serving as CEO. Alfonso Farruggia, who previously co-founded a venture-backed startup in Italy, leads the product engineering, while Sam Budd has a background in medical image computing and software engineering. The company operates in the health-tech market, specifically focusing on obstetric care. Its core business is developing artificial intelligence-powered tools for pregnancy ultrasounds to improve the speed and accuracy of medical diagnoses. Fraiya serves healthcare professionals, such as sonographers, and obstetric scanning departments within hospital settings. Its business model centers on deploying its proprietary platform to enhance service delivery for these clients. Fraiya''s product suite aims to halve examination times and improve screening. The main offering is a platform that includes several components. FraiyaScan is an accessory that connects to any ultrasound machine, providing sonographers with real-time AI assistance during scans. This device links to FraiyaHub, a cloud storage solution that streams and stores the entire scan. Th…', 'https://fraiya.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/fraiya-ultrasound/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/13/f03a5bf85621424f56cbcc3b4148c1a6.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/fraiya', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Connected Device|Recognition Technology|Health Platform|Health|Pregnancy|Ultrasound|Medical Imaging|Core AI|Spinout|Maternity|Femtech|AI for medical imaging|Woman Founder|AI Applications|Health It|DT and LS|rio ai health|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2023', '17', 3825739, 'life_sciences'),
('2dfaef6e-2481-4890-8ba7-e4b254940ad6', 'Medly AI', 'Personalised AI tutor for student exam preparation.', 'Medly AI is a London edtech company founded in 2023 by former NHS doctors and UCL medicine graduates Dr. Paul Jung (CEO) and Dr. Kavi Samra that builds a curriculum-aligned AI tutor for exam preparation. Aimed at students aged roughly 14–18 (GCSEs, IGCSEs, A-Levels, IB, with US SAT/AP expansion), the platform combines multiple specialised models with neuroscience-informed teaching, instant marking and feedback, handwriting recognition and progress tracking so learners get personalised tutoring without premium private-tutor prices. Since launching in February 2025 Medly reports rapid UK growth (hundreds of thousands of users) and grade-improvement outcomes in exam seasons; it also offers Medly Open for university students. After a February 2025 £1.7 million round led by Eka Ventures with Ada Ventures, Medly raised a €6.89 million ($8 million) Seed in August 2026 led by Felix Capital with Eka, Ada and angels, to grow the UK community, expand internationally and deepen proprietary marking and pedagogy models; it also won a UK Department for Education AI Tutoring Tools Pioneers grant. Sources: EU-Startups 19 Aug 2026.', 'https://medlyai.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/medly-ai/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/92919b1cd0d267a664586f09a3a7a512.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/medly_ai', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.523815, -0.1437048, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Education Providers|Health|Core AI|AI Applications|uk is8 digital and technologies|Education', '2023', '5', 14585581, 'life_sciences'),
('94ac8fad-214a-4aa6-a0f7-c7273207f50a', 'Lupa Pets', 'AI-powered platform streamlining veterinary practice management and client communication', 'Lupa Pets, established in London in 2023, is developing a veterinary-specific operating system to address inefficiencies in the pet care market. The company was co-founded by CEO Nicolò Frisiani, CTO Raul Lozano Martin, and COO Matei Bjola. Frisiani''s background in engineering, computer science, and strategy consulting exposed him to the technological lag in the pet industry. Martin, formerly with Meta, gained direct insight into the challenges faced by veterinarians through his sister, who is a vet in Spain. This combination of experiences spurred the creation of a unified platform to modernize clinic operations. The company''s core offering is the Lupa Operating System (OS), a B2B software-as-a-service (SaaS) platform designed for veterinary practices. It functions as an all-in-one system, integrating practice management, client engagement, and a mobile application for pet parents. This model aims to replace multiple disjointed tools with a single, integrated solution, thereby reducing technology spending for clinics. Revenue is generated through subscriptions to the Lupa OS. Lupa OS automates administrative tasks such as scheduling, clinical documentation, billing, and inventory management. A key feature is its AI co-pilot, "Jerry," which offers diagnostic suggestions and operational insights to support clinical decision-making. Another component, Lupa Notes, uses AI to transcribe consultations into structured clinical notes, a feature that can be adopted as a standalone p…', 'https://lupapets.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/lupapets/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/27/67c6416d2a602860ea15b6fca5b4145c.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/lupa_pets', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.519066, -0.1711844, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Machine Learning|Mobile app|Health Platform|Veterinary|Health|Core AI|Tech for Medical Professionals|Pets|AI Applications|AI Agents|ogr torino|rio ai health|uk is8 digital and technologies|Enterprise Software', '2023', '84', 19075750, 'life_sciences'),
('0a1f75de-8de2-4041-aecd-738d855faf68', 'Zonova', 'Antimicrobial additive technology for medical devices.', 'Zonova Technologies Ltd is a London-based medical materials company that has developed Z-ROS®, a patented antimicrobial technology embedded directly into the polymers used to manufacture medical devices. Rather than relying on surface coatings or antibiotics, Z-ROS® is engineered into the device material itself, aiming to prevent microbial colonisation and biofilm formation while avoiding the resistance pathways typically associated with antibiotic use. The company operates a licensing-led model, partnering with medical device original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) to integrate Z-ROS® into existing product lines and regulatory pathways rather than manufacturing devices itself. Initial applications focus on vascular access devices such as peripheral and central venous catheters, with planned expansion into urology, women''s health and orthopaedic devices; the technology is also being piloted in veterinary settings. Founded in 2023 by Dr Georgia Fleet and Carla Southworth, Zonova addresses two pressing healthcare challenges: hospital-acquired infections, which affect roughly one in ten patients according to the WHO, and the wider antimicrobial resistance crisis. In May 2026, the company closed a £2.1 million seed funding round led by THENA Capital to scale commercialisation, expand its patent portfolio and pursue OEM licensing partnerships. Keywords: antimicrobial technology, medical devices, infection prevention, biofilm, antimicrobial resistance, catheters, medtech, licensin…', 'https://zonovatech.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/zonovatech/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/08/285ce2317ecc8a5c91ca88814dca2be1.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/zonova', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Health|medical implants|Infections and Infectious Diseases|Biomaterials|Catheters|Sustainable Development Goals|Advanced Materials|Anti-Infectives|Woman Founder|DT and LS|rio engineering biology|uk is8 life sciences', '2023', '12', 2795441, 'life_sciences'),
('b081d168-cc82-41ca-afbb-002b6b2cbe5d', 'Chiron Digital Health', 'AI-driven self-care platform for chronic disease management', 'Chiron Digital Health Ltd is a health technology company, founded in 2023 and based in London, UK. The company was co-founded by CEO Carron Manning, CTO Davide Crescenzi, and CSO Dr. Karen Lawson, spinning out of the Founders Factory Venture Studio in December 2023. Carron Manning is a serial entrepreneur and clinical specialist physiotherapist with experience in the NHS and with professional athletes. Davide Crescenzi has a background in data science and AI, while Dr. Karen Lawson has led global technology teams at companies like Nike and holds a Doctorate in Computational Intelligence from UCL. The company offers a mobile health application that uses artificial intelligence to provide personalized self-care interventions for individuals with chronic diseases. The platform analyzes patient data profiles to recommend evidence-based, personalized self-care plans, including physical activity, nutrition, and psychological therapy. It allows users to test the impact of these interventions by tracking data from various sources, such as patient-reported outcomes, wearables, and electronic health records. The AI algorithms become more intelligent as more user data is collected, enhancing the personalization of recommendations. Chiron Digital Health operates on a B2B model, targeting healthcare payers, providers, and pharmaceutical companies, while also offering a B2C application for patients. Its business aims to improve value-based outcomes and reduce healthcare costs by empowerin…', 'https://stepshealth.co', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/steps-health-co/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/28/67c6e3a8dbe3f96e408de5141a04dd46.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/chiron_digital_health', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Mobile app|Health|Chronic Disease|Core AI|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Wearable|Woman Founder|AI Applications|rio ai health|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2023', '8', 900000, 'life_sciences'),
('48164b46-7b0d-4aa8-9122-67765a3baa33', 'LightHearted AI', 'AI-powered, non-contact cardiovascular diagnostic device', 'LightHearted AI, founded in 2023 by Dr. Lucrezia Cester and Dilip Rajeswari, is developing a medical device for the rapid, non-contact diagnosis of cardiovascular disease. The London-based company is a spin-out from the University of Glasgow and was established after the co-founders met at the Entrepreneur First accelerator. Dr. Cester is an AI Engineer and Clinical Scientist, and the core technology was developed during her PhD in AI and Biomedical Devices. Dilip Rajeswari serves as the Machine Learning engineer and DeepTech Entrepreneur. The company''s primary product is a touch-free diagnostic and monitoring device that utilizes laser-based technology, specifically remote laser Doppler vibrometry, combined with an ultrafast camera. This system shines a laser at an individual and analyzes the reflected light to detect micro-vibrations on the skin caused by heart activity. An AI-powered platform then processes this data to identify biomarkers related to cardiac function, enabling the detection of heart conditions like valve diseases and arrhythmias through clothing and from a distance in about 60 seconds. The platform generates a diagnostic report without needing expert intervention. LightHearted AI aims to revolutionize cardiac screening by providing a faster, more affordable, and accessible alternative to traditional methods like ECGs. The business model focuses on deploying this technology in primary care and community settings, allowing General Practitioners to screen pa…', 'https://lighthearted.ai', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/lightheartedai/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/722ed5e8d9ba770f18b9e873f2802a8e.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/lighthearted_ai', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507336, -0.12765, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Hardware|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Health|Cardiology and cardiovascular|Core AI|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Health Diagnostics|Tech for Medical Professionals|Hard Tech|Woman Founder|AI Applications|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI medical devices|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2023', '15', 285107, 'life_sciences'),
('ccb58428-5b3f-45d6-ac75-e1afb4dd61b8', 'Neu Health', 'Smartphone platform for Parkinson''s and dementia care', 'Neu Health is a health-tech company that spun out of the University of Oxford in 2022. Founded by Caroline Cake and Dr. Kinan Muhammed, the London-based firm aims to make modern care for Parkinson''s disease and dementia more accessible. The company is built on over a decade of research and clinical validation from the University of Oxford. Neu Health has developed a digital platform that uses a patient''s smartphone to monitor and analyze symptoms related to neurological conditions. The system combines a patient-facing app with a dashboard for clinicians. Through the app, which requires about seven minutes of use, patients perform tasks that allow the platform''s AI and machine learning algorithms to measure motor and cognitive functions, such as tremor, balance, speech, and memory. This data provides healthcare providers with objective, trackable metrics and predictive insights into disease progression, with the capability to forecast significant clinical outcomes up to 18 months in advance. The platform is designed to improve clinical outcomes by enabling more personalized and data-driven care, while also offering educational resources and support for medication adherence. The company operates on a B2B2P (business-to-business-to-patient) model, partnering with healthcare providers who then prescribe the app to their patients. In early 2025, Neu Health secured €1.9 million in funding from Oxford Science Enterprises and Cedars-Sinai Intellectual Property Company to support its…', 'https://neu.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/neu-health/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/15/4415c22a5630ff315eb604e8f8654544.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/neu_3', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.523647, -0.13975085, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Health Platform|Health|Neurology|Remote Monitoring|Alzheimers Disease|Degenerative Diseases|Core AI|Health Diagnostics|Spinout|Sustainable Development Goals|Clinical Decision Support|Physician Support Tools|Woman Founder|AI Applications|Health It|remote health monitoring|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI physician support|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2022', '22', 8918181, 'life_sciences'),
('01f7d092-b3eb-4aa2-8f1c-caf99ae895ba', 'Ambr', 'AI roleplays for workplace training', 'Ambr (Ambr AI) is a London-based B2B training platform that uses AI conversation simulations so teams can practise high-stakes workplace dialogues. The company helps enterprises build skills for sales, management, and customer conversations without real-world risk. Ambr AI offers customizable voice and conversation roleplays—covering performance feedback, price objections, escalations, and other scenarios—with instant feedback on communication style. Organizations can build scenarios in-product, commission custom simulations, or let individuals create private practice sessions, with admin reporting across teams and support for many languages. Ambr commercializes enterprise training software on a subscription model for companies that need scalable, realistic conversation practice across leadership, sales, and service functions. keywords: Ambr, Ambr AI, AMBR TECHNOLOGIES LIMITED, AI roleplay, conversation simulation, enterprise training, sales training, management training, voice AI, London', 'https://ambr.ai', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/ambrtech/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/c4d11ebc17f7c3a319815f6a2ebff6e9.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/ambr_2', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.526573, -0.0881997, 'Life sciences|Recognition Technology|Health Platform|Personal Health|Corporate Wellness|Human Resources|Health|Mental Health|Employee Benefits|Woman Founder|Enterprise Software', '2022', '14', 2391666, 'life_sciences'),
('6051ca9a-7e22-4f16-bf98-5d8fa6ab7833', 'MintNeuro', 'Low-power semiconductor chips for minimally-invasive neural implants.', 'MintNeuro is a UK-based company developing a modular platform of semiconductor chips for next-generation neural implants. The company spun out of Imperial College London in 2022, founded by CEO Dr. Dorian Haci and CTO Professor Timothy Constandinou, leveraging over two decades of research in bioelectronics and neural interfaces. The founding team also includes Chief Scientific Officer Professor Andrew Jackson of Newcastle University and Chair of the Board Professor Tim Denison, a former VP at Medtronic. The company''s formation was a culmination of extensive academic research, with Dr. Haci''s transition from a PhD student and postdoctoral researcher to a Royal Academy of Engineering Enterprise Fellow being a key step in developing the business plan. MintNeuro addresses the core limitations of current neural implants, which are often bulky, power-hungry, and require invasive surgery. In contrast, MintNeuro''s proprietary integrated circuits are designed to be ultra-low-power, highly integrated, and significantly smaller—some as small as a peppercorn—enabling minimally invasive procedures. MintNeuro operates on a horizontal business model, positioning itself as a foundational hardware provider for the entire neurotechnology industry rather than focusing on a single therapeutic device. It partners with medical device companies, research institutions, and clinical groups to integrate its function-specific chips into a variety of active implantable medical devices (AIMDs) and brain…', 'https://mintneuro.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/mintneuro/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/05/3de6bf6fbd09bc9727a5e300fc35b233.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/mintneuro', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.51562, -0.0944509, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Hardware|Deep Tech|IoT InternetOfThings|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Health|medical implants|Neurology|Neuromodulation and Neurostimulation|Degenerative Diseases|Epilepsy|Core AI|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Spinout|Future of Computing|Brain Computer Interfaces|Semiconductor Designers and Manufacturers|AI Applications|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF biotech|NIF Crisis preparedness|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI medical devices|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based|Semiconductors', '2022', '29', 5191530, 'life_sciences'),
('cdf59516-40bb-4732-92e7-fece5a6c33c6', 'Early Health', 'Home devices for screening and early disease detection , enhancing survival rates and promoting healthier lifestyles', 'Early Health operates in the healthcare technology sector, focusing on the early detection of serious illnesses such as cancer, chronic kidney disease, and diabetes. The company serves individuals who seek proactive health monitoring and early diagnosis from the comfort of their homes. Early Health''s business model revolves around the development and sale of user-friendly, aesthetically pleasing medical devices that integrate seamlessly into daily routines. These devices provide critical health insights, enabling users to make timely lifestyle changes and seek prompt medical treatment, thereby improving survival rates and overall health outcomes. The company generates revenue through the direct sale of these devices and potentially through partnerships with healthcare providers and insurers. Early Health leverages cutting-edge technology and data science to create evidence-based solutions, aiming to democratize access to advanced medical diagnostics. The market it operates in includes health-conscious consumers, patients with chronic conditions, and healthcare professionals seeking reliable monitoring tools. Keywords: early detection, home healthcare, medical devices, chronic illness, health insights, proactive monitoring, user-friendly, data science, biosensors, evidence-based, survival rates.', 'https://earlyhealth.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/early-health-limited/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/06/27/81c2b89ff7051ce54e16a58d5f549c35.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/early_health_2', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.53124, -0.1175506, 'Life sciences|IoT InternetOfThings|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Health|Home Healthcare|Medical & Healthcare|Screening|Biosensors|Chronic Disease|Health Diagnostics|Diagnosis and Monitoring|Preventive Care|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2022', '37', 6049586, 'life_sciences'),
('49c213a6-4e52-46bb-99e9-f95898ae4611', 'Isomorphic Labs', 'An artificial intelligence company to discover new drugs', 'Isomorphic Labs, founded in 2021, is an AI-driven company dedicated to revolutionizing drug discovery and development. By leveraging the groundbreaking advancements from Google DeepMind, such as AlphaFold, Isomorphic Labs aims to apply machine learning and computational methods to tackle complex biological challenges. The company operates at the intersection of AI, biotechnology, and medicine, focusing on developing predictive and generative models to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of drug design and medical research. Supported by the robust infrastructure of Alphabet Inc., Isomorphic Labs combines the agility of a startup with substantial resources and expertise. The leadership team, including notable figures like Sir Demis Hassabis and Colin Murdoch, drives the company''s mission to transform how medicine is discovered and delivered. Their approach integrates deep learning, reinforcement learning, and other advanced AI techniques to innovate within the life sciences, aiming to bring better therapeutic solutions to market more swiftly and accurately.', 'https://isomorphiclabs.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/isomorphic-labs/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/b32145c32425bb88f7fcc0a04b7e52af.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/isomorphic_labs', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.537323, -0.12307775, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Machine Learning|BioTechnology|Health|Drug Development|Core AI|Verified Unicorns and $1B Exits|Tech for Biotech and Pharma|AI Drug Discovery|BIA Techbio UK|Techbio|CompBio|Techbio Drug Discovery|AI Applications|Digital Pharma|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF Crisis preparedness|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|rumoured round|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|comp bio and chem|science-based', '2021', '456', 2046741606, 'life_sciences'),
('36f9fef2-3870-4834-8660-8fd05ce0d003', 'Samphire Neuroscience', 'Wearable neurotechnology for drug-free menstrual symptom relief', 'Samphire Neuroscience is a UK-based medical technology company founded in 2021 by CEO Dr. Emilė Radytė and COO Alex Cook. The company focuses on developing neuroscience-driven, non-invasive solutions to address women''s health issues, particularly those related to the menstrual cycle. The founders'' paths converged at the University of Oxford. Dr. Radytė, a neuroscientist with degrees from Harvard and a PhD from Oxford, became frustrated by the lack of effective, side-effect-free options for menstrual symptoms while researching neurostimulation for mental health conditions. This led to the idea of applying the same science to the brain''s response to hormonal changes. Cook, who has a background in law and finance, provides operational and legal expertise. The company was named after the resilient samphire plant, which thrives in harsh environments, symbolizing the women the company aims to support. The company''s flagship product is the Nettle™, a CE-certified wearable headband that uses a well-researched technology called transcranial direct current stimulation (tDCS). This non-invasive device delivers gentle electrical currents to specific brain regions to alleviate menstrual pain, mood swings, and brain fog without the use of drugs or hormones. Users wear the headband for 20 minutes daily for five days leading up to their period. Clinical data has shown significant symptom relief, with a 53% average reduction in pain and a 34% improvement in mood symptoms. The Nettle™ device …', 'https://samphireneuro.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/samphireneuro/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/44c1bf26448211982cdaa5d27cd82da2.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/samphire_neuroscience', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.518448, -0.1421236, 'Life sciences|Pharmaceutical|Health Platform|Health|Neurology|Neuromodulation and Neurostimulation|Femtech|Sustainable Development Goals|Wearable|Menopause|Menstrual Health|Hard Tech|Woman Founder|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2021', '12', 6187363, 'life_sciences'),
('462b5e76-e3eb-4a7b-a913-5460876695ba', 'Calla Lily Clinical Care', 'Leak-free vaginal drug delivery platform for fertility', 'Calla Lily Clinical Care is a British medical technology company established in 2021, operating as a certified B-Corporation based in London. The company was co-founded by Dr. Lara Zibners, a board-certified pediatrician, and Thang Vo-Ta, a former Goldman Sachs private equity investor and serial entrepreneur. The inspiration for the company stemmed directly from Dr. Zibners'' personal experiences with seven challenging IVF cycles, which highlighted the significant patient need for a better drug delivery method than existing painful injections or inconvenient, leaky pessaries. Vo-Ta had previously developed an FDA-cleared leak-free period care product, and the two partnered to repurpose this technology for critical women''s health applications. The company''s core product is the Callavid®, a patented, FDA-cleared drug-delivery platform designed to provide a leak-free, convenient, and dosage-confident method for administering vaginally-delivered medications. Similar to a tampon, the device uses a flexible, biocompatible polymer and an absorbent mini-liner to hold a therapeutic in place, ensuring proper absorption while preventing leakage and mess. This design aims to improve clinical outcomes and the patient experience by reducing variability in drug absorption and alleviating the stress associated with current treatments. Initially, Calla Lily is focused on a 400mg progesterone Callavid for women undergoing IVF and for the prevention of miscarriage, addressing a market with incr…', 'https://callali.ly', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/calla-lily-clinical-care/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/b27d6e0657a47147b80e7a202f1840fd.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/calla_lily_clinical_care', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.546062, -0.1785842, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Fertility|Health|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Femtech|Drug Delivery Systems|B Corp|Woman Founder|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2021', '28', 3511963, 'life_sciences'),
('46ea6b6f-1cb8-4a2f-bcb0-c54300cc997e', 'Precision Cardiovascular', 'Precision’s data platform, backed by unique measures and powerful AI, enhances digital health systems to enable remote management of cardiovascular diseases', 'Precision CV is a pioneering company in the digital health sector, focusing on advanced remote monitoring solutions for cardiovascular diseases. The company addresses the critical gap in post-hospital heart monitoring, which often leads to a decline in patient health and outcomes. Precision CV''s innovative platform leverages powerful AI and unique measures to provide accurate, objective insights, enabling patients to manage their health proactively and confidently from home. The company''s primary clients include healthcare providers, hospitals, and clinics that aim to improve patient quality of life through comprehensive data collection and early intervention. Operating in the global cardiovascular care market, Precision CV''s business model revolves around offering a subscription-based service for its monitoring platform, generating revenue through recurring fees from healthcare institutions. The company is dedicated to revolutionizing cardiac health management by introducing user-friendly, cutting-edge solutions that enhance remote patient care and reduce the economic burden of heart failure-related illnesses. Keywords: AI-powered, remote monitoring, cardiovascular health, proactive management, digital health, heart failure, patient outcomes, healthcare providers, subscription-based, data-driven.', 'https://precision-cv.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/precision-cv/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/09/e48dd5e2876431986598c728bc684fd9.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/precision_cardiovascular', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.554478, -0.4767094, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Health|Patient Care|Core AI|Spinout|AI Applications|Digital Care|remote health monitoring|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI medical devices|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2021', '16', 2142564, 'life_sciences'),
('99cc7f88-6aae-4db6-9eb7-f75d24f717dd', 'Unfabled', 'Wellness platform offering curated, sustainable health and hygiene products for women’s life-stages', 'Launched in February 2021, Unfabled is the first marketplace for menstrual wellness. We curate sustainable and ethical brands for period care, period symptoms, and for self-care at any time of the month. We call it cycle care. Menstrual care is self-care. Period.', 'https://unfabled.co', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/unfabled/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/f0d0f1ce452e3feae8e68de526aa9022.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/unfabled', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.51724, -0.1794394, 'Life sciences|Medical Devices|Health Platform|Health|Wellness Beauty|Femtech|Sustainable Development Goals|Tech for Patients|Menstrual Health|Woman Founder|Digital Care|uk is8 life sciences', '2021', '10', 2499999, 'life_sciences'),
('16659e09-8e3b-4c01-b081-9f7aac862d3e', 'Valink Therapeutics', 'Creating custom biologics using a modular approach', 'Valink Therapeutics is a biotechnology company specializing in the development of bispecific antibody drug conjugates for the treatment of solid tumors. The company leverages its proprietary 5D Combinatorial Drug Discovery Platform to rapidly design and build libraries of drug candidates using modular components such as antibody fragments and small molecules. This approach allows for the creation of next-generation cancer treatments that are both specific and effective, targeting two cellular markers simultaneously to distinguish malignant from healthy tissue. Valink Therapeutics serves the oncology market, focusing on providing innovative solutions for cancer treatment. The business model involves the development and commercialization of these advanced therapeutics, generating revenue through partnerships, licensing agreements, and direct sales. Keywords: bispecific antibodies, drug conjugates, solid tumors, cancer treatment, modular design, 5D platform, oncology, biotechnology, rapid drug design, antibody engineering.', 'https://valinktx.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/valinktx/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/11/01/a4217596bfb210c6ae65748adcc77fef.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/liliumx', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.52133, -0.20278408, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Drug Development|Core AI|Spinout|Tech for Biotech and Pharma|AI Drug Discovery|BIA Techbio UK|Techbio|Techbio Drug Discovery|AI Applications|Digital Pharma|YC W21|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2021', '30', 22979247, 'life_sciences'),
('df9a5b98-46d6-4c68-a0c0-907d0f831171', 'Scarlet', 'EU & UK certification for AI medical devices', 'Scarlet is a startup that operates in the healthcare technology sector, specifically focusing on the certification of Software Medical Devices. The company has identified a gap in the market where the current regulatory environment is not adequately equipped to handle the rapidly evolving field of health and medicine software. To address this, Scarlet has developed a framework that enables both manufacturers and regulators to build and monitor software products in a scalable and continuous manner. The company''s primary clients are manufacturers of Software Medical Devices and regulatory bodies. By providing a platform for the efficient certification of these devices, Scarlet helps to expedite the process of getting life-saving technology to the people who need it. This not only ensures better and safer products reach more patients, but also contributes to the broader goal of making healthcare more accessible and affordable for everyone, everywhere. Scarlet''s business model is service-based. They make money by offering their certification framework to manufacturers. Interested parties can register on their website to schedule a call or a demo, and to receive news and updates from the company. Keywords: Healthcare Technology, Software Medical Devices, Certification, Regulatory Compliance, Scalable Solutions, Continuous Monitoring, Accessible Healthcare, Affordable Healthcare, Service-Based Business Model, Life-Saving Technology.', 'https://scarlet.cc', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/scarlet-comply/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/cdf296125831f2946687e0751f86d535.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/scarlet1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.516453, -0.1088236, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Medical Devices|Health|Core AI|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Hard Tech|AI Applications|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|Enterprise Software', '2020', '103', 58636343, 'life_sciences'),
('1be7bbcd-e3e1-4817-a44b-3ff38b76b920', 'Salutare', 'Creates software so that patients are not lost in the system', 'If medical error was a disease, it would be the third commonest cause of death in the western world. What causes so much error? Clinicians have so many tasks to manage patients safely. We are dependent on inefficient, error-prone, and expensive manual work for monitoring and referrals. Everyone is overwhelmed by the growing volume of patients, changing clinical guidelines, and inconsistent data. Salutare writes software so that patients don''t get lost in the healthcare system. Salutare ONE is software-as-a-service (SaaS) that joins up clinicians with clinicians and gives patients control over how they access and manage their health data. It makes referral for specialist care easy, such as from secondary care to a tertiary specialist centre or from a clinician to a multi-disciplinary team. It organises the monitoring of long-term patients and automatically orders required blood or radiological investigations. This takes the regulated, recurring, and consistent administrative work out of clinicians'' tasks and automates them so clinicians can focus on patient care. Operationally over time, it assembles a detailed and organized patient database for hospitals to improve clinical research and clinical excellence. Salutare ONE Referral - digital MDT referral platform for Cancer MDTs or specialists which can work with any EPR, ONE Monitor - a monitoring platform for long-term conditions that can release 20-30% of outpatient appointments when coupled with PIFU (patient initiated foll…', 'https://salutare.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/salutare-group/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/92b90b0816db5b10daab4c0ae7e7ae42.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/salutare', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.50735, -0.1277583, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Big Data|Mobile app|Health Platform|Health|Core AI|Virtual Assistant|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Clinical Decision Support|Physician Support Tools|Health Office Tools|AI Applications|uk is8 digital and technologies|Enterprise Software', '2020', '32', 1399999, 'life_sciences'),
('84403ef8-8a32-454f-86f6-589494e50292', 'PreActiv', 'Offers a digital platform delivering personalised prehabilitation programmes to optimise patient health before surgery', 'PreActiv is a UK-based healthtech startup that provides prehabilitation services to patients preparing for surgery. Prehabilitation, a preparation phase before surgery, has been proven to reduce surgical complications and shorten hospital stays, leading to significant cost savings for healthcare providers. PreActiv''s doctor-designed, evidence-based programmes are tailored to individual patients and can be accessed from the comfort of their homes, eliminating the need for hospital visits. The company''s technology creates bespoke programmes that adapt to the patient''s needs and abilities, using behavioural change methods to maximise adherence. This approach not only reduces pressure on healthcare providers but also contributes to the UK''s net-zero targets by eliminating travel-related emissions. PreActiv''s services are 84% cheaper than in-person or telemedicine programmes, making them accessible to a wider range of patients and helping to reduce health inequalities. The company''s platform can be accessed anytime and from anywhere, further enhancing its accessibility. The startup operates in the UK healthcare market, serving patients who are preparing for surgery. Its business model is based on providing cost-effective, accessible, and effective prehabilitation services that improve patient outcomes and reduce healthcare costs. The company generates revenue by charging for its prehabilitation programmes. The National Health Service (NHS) has mandated the implementation of preha…', 'https://preactiv.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/preactiv/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/04/c2d11a95d6811f11f947a0692184a7fa.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/preactiv', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.5148, -0.1235294, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Surgery|Patient Care|Physiotherapy|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Tech for Patients|Woman Founder', '2020', '14', 871628, 'life_sciences'),
('a2be59ee-e417-4a0f-bd6d-efac2194a64e', 'Cellsway', 'Microfluidic liquid biopsy platform for isolating tumor cells', 'Cellsway, established in 2020 by co-founders Prof. Dr. Haluk Külah (CEO), Dr. Özge Zorlu (CTO), Assoc. Prof. Dr. Ebru Özgür (CSO), and Tayfun Akin, is a company focused on developing microfluidic systems for biomedical applications. The firm''s core product is a liquid biopsy platform that isolates rare Circulating Tumor Cells (CTCs) from a simple blood sample, offering a minimally invasive alternative to traditional surgical biopsies for cancer diagnostics and research. This method allows for real-time monitoring of cancer, safer and more frequent sampling, and better patient profiling. The company''s proprietary technology is based on a patent-pending microfluidic chip, tagCTC-ENR, that separates intact CTCs from blood cells based on size. This label-free, antigen-independent enrichment process ensures the capture of a wide variety of CTCs, which can then be used for numerous downstream analyses, including DNA, RNA, and protein analysis. Cellsway provides a fully automated device and various test panels, such as those for identifying CTCs and detecting hormone receptors (ER, PR, HER2) and PD-L1 biomarkers, which are crucial for guiding personalized cancer therapy. The system is designed for use in service laboratories, featuring a user-friendly, automated operation. Headquartered in Nether Alderley, United Kingdom, with operations in Ankara, Turkey, Cellsway targets clinicians and researchers in the oncology field. The company has raised approximately $4.23 million in fundin…', 'https://cellsway.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/cellsway/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/94338374eb5509be49e099ad41ec5916.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/cellsway', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.62141, -0.1057891, 'Life sciences|Hardware|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Testing|Health|Oncology|Dermatology|Screening|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Health Diagnostics|Hard Tech|Woman Founder|Horizon Europe|medical testing|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2020', '5', 2022726, 'life_sciences'),
('a897fd30-b472-4459-9f7c-87cd0cb1f17c', 'Charac', 'Helping independent community pharmacies digitalise their services', 'Charac operates as a health-tech firm focused on the digital transformation of independent community pharmacies in the United Kingdom. The company was established in 2020 by Santosh Sahu, who serves as the CEO. Sahu''s venture into this sector was motivated by his personal experiences as a diabetic patient, where he encountered difficulties in tracking and managing his repeat prescriptions online. This firsthand experience, combined with his extensive background of over two decades in banking, IT, retail, and last-mile delivery logistics, shaped the company''s mission. The core of Charac''s business is a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS), NHS-integrated platform designed to equip pharmacies with a comprehensive digital presence. This addresses a critical gap for many independent pharmacies lacking online capabilities, allowing them to compete with larger online pharmacy chains. The platform functions as a one-stop portal for both pharmacists and patients, offering features such as automated repeat prescription ordering, appointment scheduling for services like flu jabs, access to patient records, and secure video consultations. For patients, it provides a mobile app to manage their prescriptions, book services, and communicate directly with their pharmacist. Revenue is generated through a subscription-based model offered to these independent pharmacies. Charac has secured significant strategic partnerships and funding to fuel its growth. A key milestone was a £1 million investment f…', 'https://charac.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/charac/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/21/90b23e112a847821949e42b2837b8a8f.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/charac', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.520805, -0.1080299, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Pharmacy|Tech for Medical Professionals|Hard Tech', '2020', '21', 2600000, 'life_sciences'),
('69c4f38c-d5d8-42cb-9e09-eb02b0ebc3b2', 'Augmentive', 'State-of-the-art platform powering a health and wellbeing revolution', 'Augmentive.io is a digital platform that operates in the healthcare sector, specifically in the field of professional consultation. The company''s primary service is to connect clients with the most suitable professionals for their specific needs. This is achieved through a combination of artificial intelligence (AI) and expert guidance. The AI-powered search function allows clients to cut through the noise and find the most relevant professionals, while the expert guidance ensures a seamless journey throughout the entire care pathway. The company serves a wide range of clients, from individuals seeking personal consultations to professionals looking to manage and grow their practice. The business model is centered around a free 15-minute consultation, which serves as a compass to guide clients to the most compatible specialist for their needs. This is followed by a responsive call-back service, which offers expert support at every step of the process. Augmentive.io makes money by facilitating these connections between clients and professionals. The ease of booking appointments, likened to ordering a Deliveroo, and the state-of-the-art system that ensures a seamless and secure journey, are key selling points that attract and retain clients. In summary, Augmentive.io is a digital platform that uses AI and expert guidance to connect clients with the most suitable professionals in the healthcare sector, offering a seamless and secure journey from consultation to appointment. Key…', 'https://augmentive.io', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/augmentive/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/18/919e3c5606c3dc356d02f0a90d42c80f.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/augmentive', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.4938, -0.1481197, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Health Platform|Psychology|Health|Wellness Beauty|Workforce Management|Mental Health|Telemedicine|Tech for Patients|Physician Support Tools|Hard Tech|Health It|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2020', '34', 2436270, 'life_sciences'),
('7d54036f-57df-4f3f-8150-514947d75abd', 'Basecamp Research', 'AI protein and therapeutic design from biodiversity-scale genomic data', 'Basecamp Research is a London biotechnology company founded in 2019 by Dr Glen Gowers and Dr Oliver Vince that trains foundational biological AI models on proprietary genomic data collected through partnerships in more than 30 countries. Its knowledge graph and BaseData protein corpus underpin the Eden model family for protein and DNA sequence design, including BaseFold structure prediction and aiPGI for programmable gene insertion, with a therapeutic focus on in vivo cell therapy that aims to reprogram patient cells inside the body. The company collaborates with pharmaceutical, research and industrial partners and cites preclinical progress across multiple disease areas. Funding includes a $20 million Series A (2022) and $60 million Series B (2024); in September 2026 Basecamp closed a $140 million Series C led by S32, with NVentures (NVIDIA), Anthropic’s Anthology Fund, Catalio, the NATO Innovation Fund, Rockefeller, European Tech Collective, the UK Sovereign AI Fund and returning investors Firebrand, River Capital King Philanthropies and Redalpine — bringing total funding to about $225 million to train next-generation models and advance AI-designed therapeutics toward the clinic. Sources: Tech.eu 23 Sep 2026.', 'https://basecamp-research.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/basecamp-research-bcr/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/74f651a6f9d12f13f90dd0e8d313b59e.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/basecamp_research', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.524338, -0.1062815, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Deep Learning|BioTechnology|Health Platform|Health|Genetics and genomics|Core AI|Synthetic Biology|Genome Engineering|Sustainable Development Goals|Tech for Biotech and Pharma|Biodiversity|Climate Tech|Biodiversity Tracking|Blue Economy|AI Drug Discovery|CompBio|Techbio Drug Discovery|AI Applications|Climate Adaptation|Digital Pharma|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF biotech|NIF Crisis preparedness|proteomics|DT and LS|uk rio|rio engineering biology|rio Synbio in Life Sciences|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|comp bio and chem|science-based|nt', '2019', '76', 166666600, 'life_sciences'),
('078ff2fb-6f53-4a38-a7a8-03df63227df7', 'Sava', 'Minimally invasive continuous glucose monitors', 'Sava Technologies Ltd. is a London-based health technology company working to shift healthcare from a reactive to a preventative and data-driven model. Founded in 2019 by bioengineers Renato Circi and Rafaël Michali, the company emerged from their work at Imperial College London. Both founders were passionate about personal health monitoring and recognized the limited access individuals have to their own molecular health data. Their research in the lab that invented modern glucose strip technology provided them with a deep understanding of the potential and limitations of existing biosensing technologies. The company is developing a wearable biosensor platform designed to detect and continuously monitor multiple biomarkers in the interstitial fluid just beneath the skin. This proprietary technology utilizes a multi-molecule microsensor that transmits real-time health insights to a user''s smartphone. Sava''s approach is designed to be minimally invasive, painless, and more affordable than many current solutions on the market. The platform''s core technology consists of a smart, connected wearable patch that streamlines data delivery, making health insights effortlessly accessible. Sava''s initial product is a Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM) aimed at the expanding diabetes management market, which is valued at over $11 billion. Unlike filament-based systems, Sava''s device uses several 1mm microneedles, which aims to provide a less intimidating user experience and reduce manufact…', 'https://sava.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/savahealth/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/04/004eba8b11318f269feceadb754f9d13.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/sava_3', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.520473, -0.10071291, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|Mobile app|IoT InternetOfThings|Medical Devices|Diabetes|Health|Remote Monitoring|Biosensors|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Health Diagnostics|Metabolism|Wearable|Sensor Tech|remote health monitoring|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI medical devices|uk rio|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2019', '171', 47727254, 'life_sciences'),
('a1d8aa80-db42-435f-b033-9c9dc4a2b415', 'Hormona', 'An app and personalized programs to help women understand and live in harmony with their hormones', 'Hormona.io is a pioneering startup that offers a comprehensive solution for women to understand and manage their hormonal health. The company operates in the health tech market, specifically focusing on women''s health. Its primary offering is an app that provides personalized, evidence-based advice to help women understand their hormones better. The app allows users to track their symptoms, receive tailored tips, and gain valuable insights into their hormonal health. In addition to the app, Hormona is also developing AI-powered at-home hormone tests that provide instant results in just 15 minutes. This allows women to track their hormone levels from the comfort of their home, eliminating the need for frequent doctor visits and lab tests. Hormona''s business model is likely based on a freemium model where basic features of the app are available for free, while advanced features and the hormone tests are available for a fee. This model allows the company to reach a wide audience while generating revenue from premium services. The app also offers a range of additional features such as personalized recipes designed for each cycle phase, daily highlights, and access to exclusive learning modules about the endocrine system, menstrual cycle, and hormones. These features are designed to help women live in sync with their bodies and make informed decisions about their health. In conclusion, Hormona.io is a unique startup that combines technology and medical science to empower women to…', 'https://hormona.io', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/hormona/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/25/117bad41db7b06d84d1be7f65cb3c5bf.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/hormona', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.52409, -0.1442329, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Wellness Beauty|Femtech|Sustainable Development Goals|Tech for Patients|Reproductive Health|Woman Founder|medical testing|remote health monitoring', '2019', '31', 13705980, 'life_sciences'),
('e52aa5c2-536a-4b8d-9719-b0b795eba17c', 'BoobyBiome', 'Breast milk synbiotic supplements for infant gut health', 'BoobyBiome is a UK-based biotechnology company founded in 2019 by Dr. Lydia Mapstone (CEO), Dr. Sioned Fôn Jones (COO), and Dr. Tara O''Driscoll (CTO). The founders, who met during their PhDs, leveraged their collective expertise in microbiology, neuroscience, chemistry, and biophysics to address rising infant diseases linked to underdeveloped gut microbiomes. The company''s mission is to provide every infant with the beneficial bacteria of breast milk, regardless of how they are fed, to support long-term health. The company is developing two main products. The first is a synbiotic supplement, a combination of probiotic microbes isolated from breast milk and prebiotic fibers. This supplement is designed to be added to formula or expressed breast milk to help establish a healthy gut microbiome in infants, particularly those who are formula-fed, born via C-section, or premature. The second product is a patented baby bottle accessory with a cartridge that removes oxygen, designed to preserve the natural microbiome in pumped and stored breast milk and extend its viability. BoobyBiome operates on a for-profit business model and aims to be the first to secure an EU-approved health claim for an infant probiotic, a key differentiator in a market of less regulated supplements. Headquartered at the Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health, BoobyBiome has established the world''s first breast milk microbiome database and biobank through collaborations with hundreds of donating mother…', 'https://boobybiome.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/boobybiome/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/09/26/3cea78cc1a07cd853c68821abffa2bd2.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/boobybiome', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.504555, -0.0971758, 'Life sciences|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Health|Medical Research|Microbiology|Woman Founder|DT and LS|rio engineering biology|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Kids', '2019', '16', 8028080, 'life_sciences'),
('db10f037-3e46-4dd5-8891-e6923163f0ea', 'Alchemab Therapeutics', 'Develops drugs by identifying naturally protective patient antibodies using three complementary processes and advanced technologies', 'Alchemab Therapeutics is a biotechnology startup that operates in the healthcare sector, specifically in the development of antibody therapeutics for difficult-to-treat diseases. The company''s unique approach involves studying the immune systems of resilient individuals, such as long-term cancer survivors, to understand how they resist or overcome disease. The company''s business model is centered around the use of adaptive immunity, which is the body''s ability to recognize and defend itself against specific infectious agents or diseases. Alchemab uses advanced scientific techniques and deep learning algorithms to identify and replicate the antibodies present in these resilient individuals. These antibodies are then used to create therapeutics that can potentially treat a wide range of diseases. Alchemab''s clients are primarily in the healthcare sector, including hospitals, clinics, and other medical institutions that treat patients with hard-to-treat diseases. The company generates revenue by developing and selling these novel antibody therapeutics. In summary, Alchemab is a pioneering biotech company that uses innovative techniques to develop new treatments for hard-to-treat diseases. By harnessing the power of the immune system and using advanced technology, the company is at the forefront of the next generation of antibody therapeutics. Keywords: Biotechnology, Healthcare, Antibody Therapeutics, Adaptive Immunity, Resilient Individuals, Deep Learning, Disease Treatment, I…', 'https://alchemab.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/alchemab-therapeutics-ltd/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/28/86e9fe097ec8312819f7097f6fbc9421.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/alchemab_therapeutics', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.49353, 0.05531, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Biotech and Pharma|AI Drug Discovery|Woman Founder|Techbio Drug Discovery|DT and LS|rio engineering biology|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2019', '74', 113684056, 'life_sciences'),
('a60fb2cd-6f19-4402-8c80-b6b60f230643', 'Relation Therapeutics', 'Using machine learning to improve drug discovery', 'RelationRx is a biotechnology startup that operates in the drug discovery market. The company aims to address the critical bottleneck in drug discovery, which is the poor understanding of the biology underlying diseases. This lack of understanding often leads to the failure of many drug candidates in trials and leaves numerous devastating diseases untreated. RelationRx''s solution to this problem is a radically different approach that uses machine learning to better understand the biology of disease and discover new therapeutics rationally. The company''s platform leverages ActiveGraph ML, a machine learning technology that has been successfully used by tech companies to solve problems in computer vision and product recommendations. However, RelationRx is the first to use this technology in drug discovery at such a large scale. With ActiveGraph ML, the company can understand the vast number of combinatorial functional relationships between genes, proteins, and drugs. RelationRx is also pioneering a "Lab-in-the-Loop" approach that integrates active learning at every step of drug discovery, from predicting cell states to validating new targets. The company uses real cells from proprietary biobanks to generate genomic data, providing direct insights into critical biological relationships. This data is then fed into the machine learning systems, which request new experiments to improve their predictive ability. The company''s business model revolves around using its platform to dis…', 'https://relationrx.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/relation-therapeutics/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/03/58acce5717d2e0b3e77ff086dd5682ea.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/relation_therapeutics', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.51719, -0.09616299, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Machine Learning|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Core AI|Tech for Biotech and Pharma|AI Drug Discovery|BIA Techbio UK|Techbio|CompBio|Hard Tech|Techbio Drug Discovery|AI Applications|Digital Pharma|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF biotech|NIF Crisis preparedness|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|comp bio and chem|science-based', '2019', '149', 105302988, 'life_sciences'),
('af6f7d74-498e-4ae1-be05-430d8705ac5d', 'Bioniq', 'AI-powered personalized supplements based on biomarker data', 'Bioniq is a health technology company founded in 2019 by Vadim Fedotov, James Hardy, Ahmad E. Dardiry, and Dr. Constantin Karuzin. Headquartered in London, the company specializes in providing hyper-personalized nutritional supplements based on an individual''s data. The concept originated from CEO Vadim Fedotov''s personal health journey as a former professional basketball player seeking to optimize his energy and performance beyond the scope of traditional medical advice. This led him to a data-driven approach to micronutrient supplementation. Bioniq operates on a direct-to-consumer subscription model, serving health-conscious individuals, wellness enthusiasts, and athletes. The company''s business model is built around two core products: Bioniq PRO and Bioniq GO. Bioniq PRO, the premium service, utilizes comprehensive blood test results to analyze over 50 biomarkers, which are then processed by a proprietary AI algorithm to create a precise, customized supplement formula. The Bioniq GO service offers a more accessible option, using an extensive online questionnaire to predict nutrient needs and generate a personalized formula. Both products are delivered as patented slow-release granules, designed for enhanced absorption compared to traditional pills. The company has built a proprietary database of over six million biochemical data points from more than 100,000 members to refine its algorithm. The company has raised a total of $31.1 million over several funding rounds, with …', 'https://bioniq.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/bioniqhs/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/96447d05be3e2d7f88d2f1edc04c05ab.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/bioniq_health_tech_solutions', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.4862, -0.1185497, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Pharmaceutical|Innovative Food|Dietary Supplements|Health|Biotechnology|Health Supplements|Core AI|Nutrition|Precision Medicine|Longevity|AI Applications|DT and LS|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Food', '2019', '52', 34606032, 'life_sciences'),
('cb9f66a4-a915-469c-a023-bbcc150d5c84', 'Scan.com', 'Private MRI Scan Without Referral | National MRI Scan', 'Scan.com is a UK- and US-based medical imaging network that connects patients, employers, health plans and digital-health apps to MRI and other diagnostic scans through a national API for search, scheduling and results, with care guides throughout. Already the UK''s largest imaging network, it expanded into the US in 2023 and reports more than 900,000 patients served globally and revenue doubling to a $165 million-plus annualized run rate. Live two-way integrations with imaging centers'' scheduling systems and EMRs, plus AI matching on availability, price and subspecialty, aim to replace fax/phone booking in a still largely offline market. In August 2026 Scan.com closed $220 million in combined financing: a $90 million Series C equity round led by Noteus Partners (with Aviva, Concord Health Partners, YZR Capital, Oxford Capital and others) plus $130 million of debt facilities from VerisFi Capital and Atempo Growth for network expansion, M&A, working capital and API/agentic AI infrastructure—equity and debt kept distinct. Sources: Scan.com press release 31 Aug 2026; Medical Device Network.', 'https://scan.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/scan.com/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/f9e4bb7c39ef22c36a2f067511a4cf4b.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/scan_com', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.512085, -0.1141211, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Wellness Beauty|Medical & Healthcare|MRI|Radiology|Medical Imaging|Health Diagnostics|Appointment|Tech for Patients', '2017', '172', 100502393, 'life_sciences'),
('c05219ce-52d1-4bae-b520-06a0f6c59a8c', 'Genomes.io', 'Secure DNA sequencing, storage and sharing platform', 'Genomes.io is a London-based biotechnology company positioning itself at the intersection of genomic data, privacy, and blockchain technology. Founded in 2018 by Dr. Mark Hahnel and Aldo de Pape, the firm directly addresses the increasing concerns over data sovereignty in the consumer genomics market. The company''s core proposition is to shift the ownership and control of sensitive DNA data from corporations back to the individual. This model stands in contrast to incumbent services that often monetize user data by selling it to third parties, such as pharmaceutical companies, without direct consent or compensation for the individual. The founders'' backgrounds are central to the company''s mission. Dr. Mark Hahnel, with a PhD in human genetics, previously founded Figshare, a platform for sharing scientific data, instilling a principle of open, yet controlled, data access into Genomes.io''s DNA. Co-founder and CEO Aldo de Pape complements this with his leadership, driving the company''s vision to democratize the genomics market. Their collective expertise addresses a market failure where individuals, upon sending their DNA for analysis, relinquish control, exposing their most personal information to potential data breaches and exploitation. Genomes.io operates a multifaceted business model. For individuals, it offers whole genome sequencing (WGS), analyzing 100% of a person''s DNA, a significant leap from the 0.02% typically analyzed by standard genotyping services. This data is …', 'https://genomes.io', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/genomes-io/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/28/4349d5bcba4314a586a74834a1a4c180.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/genomes_io', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.531815, -0.1206006, 'Life sciences|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|DNA|Genetics and genomics|Disease|Biotech and Pharma|Hard Tech|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2017', '12', 16406322, 'life_sciences'),
('25a01636-74f9-4fda-b3a6-636f12cebb97', 'ThinkSono', 'AI-assisted ultrasound at point of care to detect deep vein thrombosis within minutes', 'ThinkSono operates in the healthcare technology sector, specializing in AI-powered ultrasound guidance and training solutions. The company primarily serves non-specialist healthcare professionals, enabling them to perform accurate and efficient ultrasound examinations. ThinkSono''s core product, AutoDVT, provides real-time AI annotations that guide users through the process of capturing the correct ultrasound data. This technology is particularly useful for diagnosing Deep Vein Thrombosis (DVT) in primary care settings, reducing the need for specialist equipment and hospital visits. The business model is subscription-based, offering access to their software and cloud platform where exams can be uploaded for expert feedback and quality assessment. ThinkSono generates revenue through these subscriptions and potentially through partnerships with healthcare institutions. The market for ThinkSono''s solutions includes primary care providers, general practitioners, and healthcare institutions looking to improve diagnostic pathways and patient outcomes. By leveraging AI, ThinkSono aims to democratize access to ultrasound diagnostics, making it easier for non-specialists to perform complex examinations. Keywords: AI-powered, ultrasound, healthcare, diagnostics, DVT, primary care, non-specialists, training, cloud platform, subscription-based.', 'https://thinksono.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/thinksono/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/61b1e7f52a1c0d36127f901040cf7556.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/thinksono', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.529697, -0.0977626, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Health Platform|Health|Point of Care|Ultrasound|Medical Imaging|Core AI|EIT Health|AI for medical imaging|Physician Support Tools|Hard Tech|EIT Ecosystem|AI Applications|Horizon Europe|Health It|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI medical devices|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Enterprise Software', '2016', '23', 13914221, 'life_sciences'),
('18b7ebcd-1687-4cc7-9f35-47a59ab7299f', 'Semble', 'Heydoc is a cloud-based clinical system covering all the medical and admin needs of medical practice', 'Semble (formerly Heydoc) is a London cloud clinical and practice-management platform for private outpatient providers — coordinating the patient journey with EHR, booking, billing, telehealth and e-prescribing, plus 1,200+ integrations via Semble Connect. Founded by Christoph Lippuner and Mikael Landau, press around the raise cited more than 10 million patients served and ~1,700 customers including Nuffield Health, Welbeck and London Doctors Clinic, with growing traction in France. In June 2026 Semble raised a £30 million (€34.7 million) Series C led by Revaia, with new investor Partech and returning Mercia Ventures and Octopus Ventures participating. Capital expands into larger healthcare groups, deepens AI care-orchestration and cements the France position. Sources: Semble 4 Jun 2026; EU-Startups; Mercia.', 'https://semble.io', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/semble-health/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/3e35de085b7aacfdab88742a615553bf.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/heydoc_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.52145, -0.0816498, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Tech for Medical Professionals|Medical Practice Management|Physician Support Tools|Health Office Tools|observatoire healthtech', '2016', '159', 50833325, 'life_sciences'),
('b3aabd0d-24ba-44b3-b2aa-a6d6ca3eff58', 'ELLIPSES PHARMA', 'Accelerating development of promising oncology drug candidates', 'Ellipses Pharma is a drug development company focused on accelerating the availability of cancer medicines and treatments. The company was founded in 2015 by Professor Sir Chris Evans and Dr. Rajan Jethwa, who serve as Chairman and CEO, respectively. Sir Chris Evans is a renowned biotech entrepreneur with a track record of founding over 50 life sciences companies, including several that achieved unicorn status. The company''s business model centers on in-licensing promising clinical candidates from biotech companies, academic institutions, and pharmaceutical partners. Ellipses then leverages a unique drug development model that combines unbiased vetting of assets, uninterrupted funding, and expert oversight to accelerate clinical trials. A key component of this model is the Scientific Affairs Group, a network of over 300 global oncology key opinion leaders who provide independent, unbiased expertise to de-risk asset selection and optimize clinical trial design. This approach aims to reduce R&D costs and enhance the probability of success. Instead of seeking funding for individual trials, Ellipses capitalizes the company as a whole, ensuring that capital is allocated to in-licensed assets as needed, which streamlines the development process. Once a drug has progressed through trials and reached a key value inflection point, typically during or after Phase II, the model is to out-license the asset to larger pharmaceutical companies equipped for late-stage development and commer…', 'https://ellipses.life', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/ellipses-pharma/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/aa27ee24426c6dd8277b5d18fc3ba6db.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/ellipses_pharma', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507484, -0.1442246, 'Life sciences|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Biotech and Pharma|Hard Tech|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2015', '41', 5800002, 'life_sciences'),
('9731034b-2b45-49a6-ae4b-c6010ffe1db0', 'Flo Health', 'The #1 most downloaded women’s health app', 'Flo''s mission is to build a better future for female health by helping you harness the power of your body signals. Flo is the #1 downloaded women’s health app worldwide, with 380 million downloads and 70 million monthly active users. In the United States, 1 in 4 women (ages 18-44) use Flo. Flo is also the first purely digital consumer women’s health app to achieve unicorn status and have a valuation beyond $1 billion. With over 120+ medical experts, Flo is committed to supporting women at every stage of their health journey, from menstruation to conception, pregnancy, and menopause. It provides curated cycle and ovulation tracking, tailored health insights, daily bite-sized visual content, and a private community for users to share their questions and concerns. Flo prioritizes safety and keeps a sharp focus on being the most trusted digital source for​ ​women''s health information. Flo Anonymous Mode feature was recognized as one of TIME’s Best Inventions 2023 and also named a finalist for Fast Company’s 2023 World Changing Ideas Awards in the Rapid Response category as part of the company''s commitment to privacy. Close to 60% of monthly active users rely on Flo for over a year. The app has become a powerful force in democratizing access to personalized health information and tackles several key issues: - Bridging healthcare disparities: Flo''s pro-social program, which provides free Premium access to up to 1 billion women across 66 countries, with over 17 million subscription…', 'https://flo.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/flohealth/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/22/8f23710cd47f7fda267eb1c6eae91514.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/flo_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.52071, -0.12209385, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Machine Learning|Mobile app|Health Platform|Fertility|Health|Analytics|Quantified