('6d73f495-5a7c-4bb1-894b-21be6c3dc778', 'Elevara Medicines', 'Oral CDK4/6 inhibitor therapy for rheumatoid arthritis', 'Elevara Medicines is a clinical-stage biotechnology company developing therapies for rheumatoid arthritis (RA) and other chronic inflammatory diseases. The company was founded in 2025 and is headquartered in London, UK. Elevara was co-founded by Weatherden, a UK-based clinical advisory group, and Monograph Capital, which provided initial funding and operational support. The leadership team includes CEO Emma Tinsley and Chief Medical Officer Professor Dominique Baeten, MD, PhD. The company''s business model is centered on developing and commercializing novel therapeutics. In October 2025, Elevara secured $70 million in a Series A financing round co-led by Forbion and Sofinnova Partners, with participation from founding investors Monograph Capital and Weatherden. This capital is intended to fund the advancement of its lead candidate, ELV001, through a Phase 2 clinical trial and to support exploratory programs in other inflammatory conditions and women''s health. Elevara gained the exclusive global rights to develop, commercialize, and manufacture ELV001 from Japan''s Teijin Pharma, which had dedicated over a decade of scientific work to the program. Elevara''s lead program, ELV001, is a first-in-class oral CDK4/6 inhibitor. Unlike traditional RA treatments that broadly suppress the immune system, ELV001 selectively targets fibroblast-like synoviocytes (FLS), which are key cells contributing to joint inflammation and damage in RA. This approach is designed to be an add-on therapy f…', 'https://elevara.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/elevara-medicines/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/11/16/5a56ab18b00b472b8df1148d36c3213c.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/elevara_medicines', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health|Drug Development|Autoimmune|Inflammatory Diseases|Woman Founder|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2025', '14', 56908282, 'life_sciences'),
('8c587fe8-8c35-4b24-a96a-41df5138c414', '28X', 'Privacy-first women''s health and period tracking app.', '28X is a digital health company offering a free, privacy-focused women''s health and period tracking application. The app is designed to be accessible globally, with no subscriptions or paywalls, and operates entirely on the user''s device to ensure data privacy. This on-device processing architecture means the company does not have servers that store user data, making it impossible for the data to be leaked or subpoenaed. The company was co-founded by Amber Vodegel, who previously founded and scaled Pregnancy+ to 150 million users before selling it to Philips in 2017. After leaving Philips in 2023, Vodegel was inspired to create a health application accessible to the majority of women who cannot afford subscriptions or advanced wearables. She spent a year consulting with over 300 experts globally to refine the concept for 28X. The other co-founder is Laurent Maguire, who has over two decades of experience in designing digital experiences and believes in creating technology centered on people rather than profit. Launched in March 2026, 28X secured £1.2 million in a funding round from the Philips Foundation and 40 mission-driven angel investors. The company''s business model is modeled after Wikipedia, sustained by donations and a voluntary "pay it forward" feature rather than venture capital, which Vodegel believed would create misaligned incentives. All profits are reinvested into advancing women''s health research and education. The app provides tools for cycle tracking, sympt…', 'https://my28x.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/28x-ltd/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/04/29/25f5f43cf107c1e8c50bed3dd50ac0e6.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/28x', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Mobile app|Health Platform|Fertility|Health|Pregnancy|Core AI|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Sustainable Development Goals|Sensor Tech|Sextech|Woman Founder|AI Applications|rio ai health|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2024', '14', 1800012, 'life_sciences'),
('07b71c07-7af5-4b24-8238-0f4d88106176', 'Ternary Therapeutics', 'AI-driven design of molecular glue therapeutics.', 'Ternary Therapeutics is a London-based biotechnology company, founded in 2024 by CEO Dr. Chris Tame and CTO Dr. Andrew Potterton, pioneers in AI-driven drug discovery and targeted protein degradation. The company operates with a headquarters in London and fully-equipped labs in Stevenage. The founders and their team possess a track record that includes the delivery of multiple clinical candidates, along with numerous patents and publications in fields like structural bioinformatics and medicinal chemistry. The firm is developing a platform that aims to systematize the discovery of molecular glues, a class of small-molecule drugs that work by inducing interactions between two proteins. This approach holds the potential to address disease-causing proteins that have been considered "undruggable" by conventional medicines, which accounts for a significant portion of therapeutic targets. Ternary''s platform integrates physics-informed artificial intelligence, machine learning, and molecular modeling with rapid laboratory testing. This creates a closed-loop system where the AI models predict how proteins will behave and suggest molecules to bind them, which are then experimentally validated. The results from the lab are fed back into the system to refine and improve subsequent design cycles, shifting the discovery process from one of chance to a more deliberate engineering problem. In March 2026, Ternary Therapeutics secured £3.6 million (€4.1 million) in a seed funding round led b…', 'https://ternarytx.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/ternary-therapeutics/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/06/06/ada8341cf5378cae0aa375a27a9e5612.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/ternary_therapeutics', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Health|Drug Development|Core AI|Immune System|AI Drug Discovery|Techbio Drug Discovery|DT and LS|rio ai health|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2024', '14', 6327381, 'life_sciences'),
('b7445189-a736-4732-ba6f-c3a0d9e922e7', 'Asterix Health', 'Remote workforce solution for UK primary care', 'Asterix Health, formerly known in market materials as Remote Duty Doctor, is a modern workforce solution for UK primary care. It matches remote clinicians and handles clinical administration and triage workflows so local practices can reduce cost and waiting time while freeing GPs for more patient consultations. Asterix supports primary care providers by combining remote clinician capacity with administration and triage work that would otherwise consume local clinical time. Public materials note that Asterix GPs can be funded using ARRS in relevant settings. Customers are primary care organisations seeking scalable remote clinical support without building that capacity entirely in-house. The business model is B2B workforce and workflow support for primary care rather than a consumer telehealth brand. Asterix partners with healthcare organisations to deliver remote clinical capacity and admin relief as an operating service. keywords: Asterix Health, asterix.health, formerly Remote Duty Doctor, UK primary care, remote clinicians, GP workforce, clinical administration, triage workflows, ARRS, primary care staffing', 'https://asterix.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/asterixhealth/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/9b48e2f96ed39ea00e7b840e02ead0fc.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/asterix_health', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Electronic Health Records (EHR)|Health|Staffing|Medical Data|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Patient Triage', '2024', '24', 4253210, 'life_sciences'),
('0c7dddf9-9d96-4d18-91f5-e4201355b112', 'UzimaNexus', 'AI OS for African healthcare', 'UzimaNexus builds an operating system for African healthcare that combines clinic automation, AI patient management, secure digital health records, telemedicine, and blockchain-enabled data sharing (including UziCoin incentives) for clinics, patients, and providers. Public products and modules span appointment scheduling, AI-assisted clinical decision support, medical supplies marketplace features, smart wearables for patient data access, and the My Doktari consumer app for doctor discovery, wellness tracking, and AI health advice across Kenya and broader African markets. UzimaNexus sells digital health / clinic OS software and related apps to clinics and patients. The business model is healthtech platform SaaS and marketplace services for African healthcare. keywords: UzimaNexus, African healthcare OS, clinic automation AI, My Doktari app, uzimanexus.com, blockchain health records UziCoin, telemedicine Kenya, AI patient management Africa', 'https://uzimanexus.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/uzimanexus/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2024/10/23/740ed2221b1bea3e7c94c6e667a8daa4.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/uzimanexus', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Personal Health|Health|Health and Wellness|Woman Founder|Digital Care', '2024', '4', 90909, 'life_sciences'),
('2418af54-169b-4895-ac48-8a636ba9ead6', 'Hello Vet', 'Veterinary care with same-day appointments, transparent pricing, and unlimited WhatsApp access to clinical teams', 'HelloVet operates in the veterinary care market, providing comprehensive services for pet owners, particularly those with cats and dogs. The business model focuses on offering same-day appointments, transparent pricing, and continuous support through unlimited WhatsApp access to their clinical team. HelloVet serves a diverse clientele, including busy pet owners who require flexible scheduling and immediate advice. The company generates revenue through service fees for appointments, treatments, and specialized care such as dental cleanings, periodontal treatments, and elderly pet care. By leveraging best practices from other industries and maintaining a compassionate, professional team, HelloVet aims to reinvent veterinary care. The company is backed by long-term investors, including 17 veterinarians who have invested their own savings, underscoring their commitment to the vision and experience of the team. Keywords: veterinary care, same-day appointments, transparent pricing, WhatsApp support, dental treatments, elderly pet care, compassionate team, flexible scheduling, pet owners, long-term investment.', 'https://hellovet.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/hello-vet/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/74cdcd684f720e4327766ebfebc5787e.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/hello_vet_hellovet_co_uk', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Veterinary|Health', '2024', '72', 21000000, 'life_sciences'),
('d7e0210f-b8c3-4418-a282-8e0c4ddff9d5', 'BioOrbit', 'BioOrbit is space manufacturing company developing hardware for the large-scale crystallisation of protein drugs', 'BioOrbit is a UK-based company specializing in the manufacturing of pharmaceuticals in space. The company focuses on the large-scale crystallization of proteins for monoclonal antibodies (mAbs), with the aim of producing more effective cancer drugs. By leveraging the microgravity environment of space, BioOrbit intends to overcome some of the limitations of Earth-based pharmaceutical manufacturing. The company is preparing for pre-clinical trials in 2026 for protein crystals produced in its planned orbital factory. The primary market for BioOrbit''s products is the pharmaceutical industry, which is constantly seeking to develop more effective treatments for a variety of diseases, including cancer. The company''s business model is centered on research and development, with the ultimate goal of commercializing its space-manufactured pharmaceuticals. This involves securing partnerships with pharmaceutical companies and research institutions to further develop and test its products. Keywords: pharmaceutical manufacturing, space technology, protein crystallization, monoclonal antibodies, cancer drugs, orbital factory, pre-clinical trials, space-based research, drug development, biotechnology.', 'https://bioorbit.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/bioorbit/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/16/67097d360f32bcab2cecaadc9e6aa104.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/bioorbit', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.525906, -0.08523744, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Drug Development|Space Tech|Biotech and Pharma|In-Space Manufacturing|Esa Bic|ESA|In-Space Operations|Space Upstream|Space DT|Woman Founder|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF space|NIF Crisis preparedness|proteomics|DT and LS|uk rio|rio space|rio space manufacturing and exploration|UKis manufacturing|uk is8 advanced manufacturing|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Space', '2023', '20', 10050000, 'life_sciences'),
('d5461d5b-2c9b-4482-bd58-e28e6d898bc1', 'Punto Health', 'AI-powered digital platform for dementia, cognitive care.', 'Punto Health is a digital health company founded in London in 2023 by engineers Anna Muñoz-Farré (CEO) and Jack Eckersley (CTO). The company was established to address the challenges in dementia and cognitive decline care, inspired by Muñoz-Farré''s personal experience with her grandfather''s battle with Parkinson''s disease and Lewy body dementia. The firm is developing what it calls an "operating system for dementia care," aiming to shift the care model from reactive to proactive and personalized. The company''s business model is centered on a full-stack, multilingual AI platform that connects patients, caregivers, and clinicians. It targets healthcare providers, insurers, and the pharmaceutical industry, with plans for a direct-to-consumer offering through partnerships. Punto Health operates in the UK and Spain, with a subsidiary established in Barcelona to solidify its presence in Catalonia. The company has secured funding to accelerate product development and commercial expansion, including a pre-seed round of approximately $840,000 and a subsequent Seed round of $2.7 million (€2.3 million) co-led by Shilling VC and Plus Partners. Punto Health''s platform consists of three core products. ''PuntoTest'' is an AI-powered, speech-based digital assessment tool for the early detection and monitoring of cognitive impairment. ''PuntoCare'' is a companion mobile application for patients and caregivers, offering personalized care plans, cognitive stimulation exercises, nutritional advice,…', 'https://puntohealth.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/punto-health/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/16/c4ef5705084b680d8bc9be4e00849135.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/punto_health', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Health Platform|Health|Caregiving|Alzheimers Disease|Degenerative Diseases|Core AI|EIT Health|Woman Founder|EIT Ecosystem|AI Applications|Horizon Europe|AI Agents|Preventive Care|rio ai health|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2023', '12', 2551249, 'life_sciences'),
('c96333d4-965c-48d3-b8c6-aeea2eb85301', 'Taurhythm Therapies', 'Advanced atrial fibrillation treatment tools enhancing ablation success with real-time mapping and integration with leading technologies', 'TauRhythm Therapies is a spin-out company from the inventors of Ripple Mapping, focusing on the atrial fibrillation (AF) market. The company offers a suite of tools, including the RETROMapping system with the Tau20 EP stimulator, designed to improve the success rate of AF ablation procedures. By providing real-time mapping of cardiac activation, TauRhythm''s technology offers physicians unprecedented insights into AF, aiming to increase ablation success rates from 60% to over 90%. Supported by the British Heart Foundation, the company is conducting two randomized controlled studies and has already treated 50 patients. TauRhythm''s products are designed to integrate seamlessly with existing market-leading technologies, offering a broader scope of treatment options. Founded by doctors and engineers at Imperial College, the company leverages its expertise in both engineering and medical sciences to develop advanced medical products. The business model focuses on licensing its technology, as demonstrated by the licensing of Ripple Mapping to Johnson & Johnson. Key clients include healthcare providers and institutions involved in cardiac care and electrophysiology. Keywords: atrial fibrillation, ablation, real-time mapping, RETROMapping, Tau20 EP stimulator, Ripple Mapping, cardiac care, electrophysiology, Imperial College, British Heart Foundation.', 'https://taurhythm.com', null, 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/06/10/e7d14f62e71dcf50e1f418701b8f388b.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/taurhythm_therapies', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.372868, -0.0698502, 'Life sciences|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Health|medical implants|Cardiology and cardiovascular|Patient Care|Spinout|Surgical Equipment|Digital Care|remote health monitoring|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010', '2023', null, 354518, 'life_sciences'),
('638be57f-52b9-4741-976c-4299b7bc9c94', 'Vesalic', 'Therapeutic extracellular vesicles targeting neurodegenerative diseases', 'Vesalic, established in London on February 23, 2023, is a biotechnology company focused on developing treatments for neurodegenerative diseases. The company''s scientific basis is centered on the use of vesicles, such as extracellular vesicles (EVs), as a promising therapeutic tool. These nanometric structures are capable of transporting drugs, proteins, and genetic material across the blood-brain barrier to target specific cells and areas within the brain, which is a significant challenge in treating neurological disorders. The company''s approach is part of a broader field investigating nanotechnologies to address conditions like Alzheimer''s, Parkinson''s, ALS, and multiple sclerosis. Research in this area suggests that both biological and artificial vesicles can carry therapeutic cargoes, such as anti-inflammatory drugs or neurotrophic factors, to protect neurons and potentially slow disease progression. This method represents an advancement over some traditional therapies which primarily manage symptoms. Vesalic''s corporate structure includes several directors, among them Valeria Ricotti, John Alexander McLaren, Simon Christopher Greville Black, and Oscar Straus Schafer. The company operates in the ''Other human health activities'' sector and is registered as a private limited company in England and Wales. Keywords: neurodegenerative diseases, extracellular vesicles, drug delivery, blood-brain barrier, biotechnology, Alzheimer''s treatment, Parkinson''s treatment, therapeutic v…', 'https://vesalic.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/vesalic-limited/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/7380b468b897aa49cf305eb1a6772ec4.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/vesalic', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.501083, -0.01814768, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health|Medical Research|Research and Development|Neurology|Spinout|Woman Founder|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010', '2023', '14', 1829991, 'life_sciences'),
('0c8cb928-85ea-4aa5-9e68-8a710c068cb4', 'Oranda Therapeutics', 'Acquiring and commercialising late-stage rare disease medicines', 'Oranda Therapeutics is a pharmaceutical company founded in 2023 by Ahmed Al-Derzi and John Irwin. The company focuses on acquiring, developing, and commercializing innovative medicines for rare diseases, particularly for the European, Middle Eastern, and African (EMEA) markets. The founders bring extensive experience to the venture. CEO Ahmed Al-Derzi has over 25 years in the pharmaceutical industry, previously co-founding and leading Consilient Health from a startup to a company with €70 million in revenue and a presence in eight markets. CCO John Irwin is a veteran in commercializing high-value orphan medicines across Europe and international markets, with expertise in pricing and reimbursement. The leadership team, which includes former Malin Corporation CEO Adrian Howd, has collectively led over 20 successful European launches of rare disease medicines. Oranda''s business model centers on in-licensing and acquiring late-stage assets from other biopharmaceutical companies. It provides a commercialization platform for these partners, focusing on regulatory approval, market access, and sales. The company''s revenue will be generated through sales of these medicines, involving upfront payments, milestone achievements, and sales royalties to its partners. Oranda is currently in exclusive negotiations to license a novel treatment for hyperphagia in Prader-Willi syndrome (PWS), a genetic disorder causing insatiable hunger. This medicine is expected to enter a pivotal Phase 3 stud…', 'https://orandatherapeutics.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/oranda-therapeutics/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/cfd922e2360041fd953027f3814213bb.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/oranda_therapeutics', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.47701, -0.1465021, 'Life sciences|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Disease|Biotech and Pharma|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2023', '7', 0, 'life_sciences'),
('34d5f342-cc30-430a-95a6-f0e716081187', 'Sable Bio', 'Reinventing Drug Safety with AI-Powered Data', 'SableBio is a pioneering startup focused on revolutionizing drug safety through advanced artificial intelligence (AI) and predictive analytics. The company operates in the pharmaceutical and biotechnology sectors, serving primarily researchers and scientists involved in drug development. By leveraging cutting-edge AI technology, SableBio provides tools that help researchers make better decisions regarding drug safety, thereby accelerating the development of safe and effective medicines. SableBio''s business model revolves around offering a platform that integrates and analyzes complex and varied datasets. This platform uses AI to predict potential safety issues in drug development, providing interpretable predictions, explanations, and actionable recommendations. The company''s technology adapts to various safety scenarios, catering to different types of medical indications, modalities, and stages of drug development. This flexibility makes it a valuable tool for a wide range of clients in the pharmaceutical industry. The company generates revenue by offering subscriptions or licenses to its platform, which provides users with access to its proprietary datasets and AI-driven insights. Additionally, SableBio may offer consulting services to help clients integrate and utilize their technology effectively. Recently, SableBio successfully completed an oversubscribed pre-seed funding round, which will enable the company to expand its team and further develop its AI-enhanced data fo…', 'https://sablebio.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/sable-bio/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/fa313bdc9997bcc9a2ee523c2d53d8d9.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/sable_bio', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.553005, -0.050844, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Pharmaceutical|Health|Biotechnology|Drug Development|Core AI|Generative AI|AI Drug Discovery|genAI Applications|Techbio|CompBio|Techbio Drug Discovery|Digital Pharma|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|comp bio and chem|science-based', '2023', '15', 4243000, 'life_sciences'),
('fec54e37-bfeb-4266-84ed-7260e1aedaa5', 'VitVio', 'Track and analyze surgeries in real-time with AI and computer vision, improving efficiency, communication, and reducing delays and readmissions', 'VitVio is a pioneering startup focused on revolutionizing the healthcare industry, specifically within hospital operating rooms. The company leverages advanced artificial intelligence (AI) and computer vision technology to enhance the safety and efficiency of surgical procedures. By analyzing video feeds from operating rooms, VitVio''s system tracks the movements of staff, patients, and equipment, providing real-time insights that help eliminate bottlenecks, streamline processes, and boost overall productivity. VitVio primarily serves hospitals and healthcare providers, aiming to improve the workflow and safety of surgical teams. The platform is designed to integrate seamlessly with existing hospital systems, including Electronic Health Records (EHR), ensuring that data synchronization is smooth and hassle-free. This integration allows for immediate syncing of scheduling and patient records, making it easier for healthcare providers to access and utilize the data. The business model of VitVio is based on a subscription service, where hospitals and healthcare providers pay a recurring fee to use the platform. This model ensures a steady revenue stream while providing clients with ongoing access to the latest updates and support. VitVio also offers comprehensive training and technical support to minimize any additional workload on the hospital''s IT department. VitVio ensures the highest standards of data security with end-to-end encryption, safeguarding all processed data in th…', 'https://vitvio.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/vitvio/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/08/26/2e4886f3bb05006c471c08609c380744.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/vitvio', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.523834, -0.1435119, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Computer Vision|Medical Devices|Health|Surgery|Core AI|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|AI Applications|rio ai health|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences', '2023', '34', 7575755, 'life_sciences'),
('b3dfebef-37f6-4950-944a-76c0ceee2ffc', 'Heim Health', 'Ally Health provides on-demand clinical care tasks in the community, making it easier to access hands-on care', 'Heim Health, established in London in 2022, operates a software platform designed to coordinate and deliver clinical care directly to patients'' homes. The company, formerly known as Ally Health, was founded by Kelly Klifa (CEO), James Monico, and Sasha Tory (Chief Growth Officer). This founding team leveraged its experience from creating Testing For All, a not-for-profit COVID-19 testing service that delivered over a million at-home tests during the pandemic. The firm''s business model is centered on a B2B2P (business-to-business-to-patient) approach, partnering with healthcare organizations in both the private sector and the UK''s National Health Service (NHS). Heim Health manages the end-to-end logistics of at-home appointments for its clients, which include primary healthcare providers like Numan, Manual, and Thriva. Revenue is generated by providing this technology-driven service that enables clients to offer in-person clinical care, such as blood tests, post-operative assessments, and injections, outside of traditional hospital settings. The core of Heim Health''s service is its API-led platform that sources and deploys skilled nurses and healthcare practitioners based on qualifications, skills, and location. A key feature is the use of ''last-mile'' delivery-inspired algorithms to optimize practitioners'' routes and schedules, which increases the number of patients that can be seen and has been reported to reduce patient waiting times by up to 85%. For patients, the platform…', 'https://heim.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/heimhealth/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/24/fa92a399b67717e4c86cb4427871c753.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/ally_health_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.514805, -0.1235196, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Home Healthcare|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Tech for Patients|Physician Support Tools|Woman Founder', '2022', '45', 4700000, 'life_sciences'),
('77700d20-da3c-4f4d-9b1f-47abae8b8dfd', 'Plan Your Baby', 'A telehealth clinic offering fertility treatment, pregnancy monitoring, and psychological support, helping reduce IVF cycles with timely diagnoses', 'Plan Your Baby, founded in 2021 and headquartered in London, operates as a fertility and pregnancy telehealth clinic. The company was established by Marija Skujina, a Certified Fertility Nurse Specialist, whose vision was to provide high-quality, accessible fertility care. Skujina''s background as an assisted reproductive technology practitioner and sonographer, with nearly 13 years of experience in a prominent fertility clinic, shaped the company''s patient-centric approach. The clinic provides a range of paid services aimed at individuals and couples navigating fertility challenges. Its business model centers on offering remote consultations, fertility assessments, and personalized treatment plans, thereby reducing the need for frequent travel and associated costs for patients. Plan Your Baby generates revenue through fees for consultations with specialists, as well as for various tests and treatments. The company has also received funding from angel investors and accelerator programs, including Femovate and FemTech Lab. Core services include fertility assessments for both men and women, non-invasive treatments, support for In Vitro Fertilization (IVF), egg freezing, and pregnancy monitoring. A key aspect of their service is the ability to conduct blood tests and ultrasound scans at over 400 partner locations across the UK, enhancing convenience for their clients. The company offers end-to-end care, from initial testing and diagnosis to treatment and early pregnancy support,…', 'https://planyourbaby.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/plan-your-baby/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/03/15/42207c3a343db245d6f39d66f8d0e3a5.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/plan_your_baby', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Mobile app|Health Platform|Fertility|Health|Pregnancy|Telemedicine|Specialist Clinics|Maternity|Femtech|Sustainable Development Goals|Reproductive Health|Remote Patient Care|Woman Founder', '2022', '15', 250000, 'life_sciences'),
('70f41bbd-28b2-439d-836d-bb88370c5970', 'Talamo', 'Digital screening platform for identifying specific learning difficulties', 'Talamo provides a digital platform for identifying Special Educational Needs (SEN), with an initial focus on dyslexia. The company was incorporated on November 1, 2021, and its mission is to democratize access to SEN identification and support. The founders are Jamie Wace (CEO), Leo Thornton (Product), and Sophie Dick (Operations). Wace''s personal experience with dyslexia was the inspiration for the company''s creation. Talamo''s core product is a digital screener that can be used by schools and parents to assess children for signs of learning needs. The test, designed for children aged 7-16, takes under 45 minutes to complete and can be administered without a specialist. For schools, the platform allows for screening entire classes to identify at-risk learners early and generate evidence-based reports. For parents, it offers an at-home test that provides a personalized report with clear next steps. The screener assesses cognitive areas such as phonological awareness, visual ability, and reading speed to map a child''s cognitive profile. The business operates on a credit-based model for schools, where they purchase credits to conduct assessments. The platform is currently used in over 650 schools in the UK. Talamo aims to expand its platform to test for a wider range of SEN conditions and has set a goal to screen one million children by 2028. Keywords: Special Educational Needs, SEN identification, dyslexia screening, digital assessment, edtech, learning difficulties, student a…', 'https://talamo.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/talamouk/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/28/19fb2b433b377e3b7d50c456989aa2c2.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/talamo_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.46339, -0.1148023, 'Life sciences|Health|Adaptive Learning|K-12|Assessment and Credentialing|Education', '2021', '11', 254961, 'life_sciences'),
('e9867f67-1f44-4f2f-80e1-a1e1dad7c1fc', 'Opto Health', 'Digital triage and patient streaming for emergency care.', 'Opto Health provides a digital triage and patient-streaming platform designed to manage patient flow in urgent and emergency care settings within the UK''s National Health Service (NHS). The company was incorporated in February 2022. The leadership team includes CEO & Co-founder Krista Burslam-Dawe, an experienced emergency nurse with over 20 years in senior clinical roles, and Co-founder Edd Royal, who has a background in technology and digital marketing. The company''s core product is a SaaS platform that addresses emergency department crowding and long waiting times by standardizing and automating the initial patient assessment process. Patients arriving at an emergency department can use their own device or an on-site tablet to self-register and complete a symptom-led questionnaire. This process, which takes under five minutes, generates an acuity score and a suggested care pathway, allowing clinical staff to prioritize high-urgency patients immediately while streaming others to the most appropriate service. The system is designed not to replace clinicians but to act as a ''force multiplier'', freeing up nursing staff from administrative triage to focus on direct patient care. The platform is a Class I UK MHRA/UKCA medical device and is interoperable with core NHS systems, including the NHS Spine, to ensure seamless integration. The technology aims to deliver significant operational benefits; modelling for a mid-sized department suggests it can release up to 28 nursing hours…', 'https://optohealth.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/optohealth/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/08/26/69d380c859ec8f4955a2a1aeae7812fa.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/opto_health', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Critical medical care|Medical Data|Hospital Logistics|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Patient Triage', '2021', '28', 562057, 'life_sciences'),
('858ce9cf-66a9-4833-a182-c475076b3371', 'JAAQ for Business', 'AI-powered mental wellbeing activation for enterprise clients.', 'JAAQ (Just Ask A Question) is a London clinically governed digital health and engagement platform founded in 2021 by Danny Gray that embeds a library of more than 10,000 clinically reviewed mental health videos into insurer, employer and healthcare digital journeys. Partners license content into their own products or a hosted JAAQ experience; conversational AI guides users to relevant videos without diagnosing or replacing care, with anonymised topic analytics for enterprise wellbeing programmes. Deployments cover more than 1.5 million eligible lives with partners such as Bupa, NatWest and Nationwide. In March 2026 JAAQ raised a €15 million (£13 million) Series A from Meridian Health Ventures, Fuel Ventures, Bolt Angels and Guinness Ventures, appointing Alex Packham as CEO to scale enterprise partnerships, deepen clinical infrastructure and enter the US. Sources: EU-Startups 23 Mar 2026.', 'https://jaaq.app', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/jaaq/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/04/29/3a935cb4eface266105cce66aa5b18f9.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/jaaq_for_business', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Health Platform|Corporate Wellness|Psychology|Health|Sports|Mental Health|Core AI|MLops|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2021', '66', 16563509, 'life_sciences'),
('d74a6a39-399f-444b-b065-f66d56a42230', 'Captur', 'Visual AI for real-time operational compliance verification', 'Captur is a quality control automation platform that utilizes visual AI to verify operational compliance in real-time, helping supply chains reduce risks as they expand. Founded in London in 2020 by Charlotte Bax, the company provides a smart camera solution that can be embedded into client mobile applications. This technology performs on-device AI computation, allowing for immediate feedback and issue detection without cloud-related lag. Charlotte Bax, who participated in the Google for Startups Female Founder program, founded Captur after experiencing firsthand the difficulties companies faced in adopting image-based AI. Her background includes founding the Deep Learning Computer Vision meetup in London and working at an enterprise AI startup, which provided her with insights into the extensive manual work required for AI model implementation. This experience drove the development of Captur’s solution, which is designed for easy implementation by product teams with minimal developer involvement. The company''s business model is subscription-based, offering tiered plans (Pro, Team, Scale-Up, and Enterprise) that provide a certain number of "verified captures" per month. The platform''s core product is its API and SDKs that enable a smart camera within a company''s mobile app. This tool uses edge AI to analyze images locally on a smartphone, providing real-time verification against a company''s specific business logic. Key features include image quality checks, object detection,…', 'https://captur.ai', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/captur-ai/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/d52a94f7eca41e721a4def7a56316571.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/captur_', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.51915, -0.1401404, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Pharmaceutical|Health|Biotechnology|Core AI|Hard Tech|Woman Founder|AI Applications|DT and LS|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Enterprise Software', '2021', '32', 8160000, 'life_sciences'),
('43db5836-3b4c-41e1-b746-495dfd6a3397', 'Hypervision Surgical', 'AI-powered hyperspectral imaging for real-time surgical guidance', 'Hypervision Surgical Limited is a medical technology company that provides an advanced surgical imaging and data analytics platform. The company was founded in 2020 as a spin-out from King''s College London by a team of clinicians and experts in medical imaging and artificial intelligence, including CEO Michael Ebner, CSO Tom Vercauteren, Clinical Lead Jonathan Shapey, and Board Director Sebastien Ourselin. The core of its offering is the HYPERSNAP® Surgical System, which combines hyperspectral imaging (HSI) and artificial intelligence to provide real-time, computer-assisted tissue analysis during surgery. This technology makes invisible tissue characteristics visible to the surgeon without the need for contact or contrast agents. The system is capable of wide-field tissue differentiation to identify tumors, normal tissue, and critical structures like nerves and blood vessels, and can assess tissue perfusion. The goal is to improve surgical precision, speed, and patient safety by providing surgeons with objective, data-driven information for better decision-making. The company''s business model focuses on creating a hardware-agnostic software solution that can integrate into existing surgical workflows, including minimally invasive, robotic, and microscopic surgeries. Having secured U.S. FDA 510(k) clearance and UKCA marking for its system, Hypervision Surgical is targeting the healthcare market in Europe and the United States. It is conducting clinical evaluation studies in c…', 'https://hypervisionsurgical.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/hypervisionsurgical/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/28/0405e3167426a8e6caa196eee9a0c3bb.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/hypervision_surgical', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.49555, -0.12008255, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Health|Oncology|Surgery|Medical Education|Medical Imaging|Core AI|Spinout|Surgical Equipment|Clinical Decision Support|AI for medical imaging|Physician Support Tools|Treatment Assistance|Hard Tech|AI Applications|Health It|AI Agents|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI medical devices|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2021', '31', 23849976, 'life_sciences'),
('f5b6f4e1-7c3e-4d51-87ab-aaf9675fd846', 'Endlyz Therapeutics', 'Developing therapeutics to restore endo-lysosomal function in neurodegeneration', 'Endlyz Therapeutics is a biotechnology company founded in 2021 that develops disease-modifying therapeutics for Parkinson''s disease and other dementias. The company''s mission is to restore endo-lysosomal function to halt neurodegeneration. Endlyz was founded by Dr. Joanna Wolak (CEO), Professor Richard Wade-Martins, Professor John Davis, and Professor Peter Vangheluwe, emerging from work initiated by SV Health Investors'' Dementia Discovery Fund (DDF) and Oxford University. The company''s core focus is on developing small-molecule therapeutics that target lysosomal transporters ATP13A2 and ATP10B. These transporters are critical for maintaining the health of neurons; their dysfunction is a key driver of neurodegeneration. The lead program involves small molecule potentiators of ATP13A2, which is encoded by the PARK9 gene linked to Parkinson''s disease. This approach aims to slow or stop disease progression, a significant shift from merely treating symptoms. The initial clinical focus will be on genetic subsets of Parkinson''s, with plans to expand to sporadic Parkinson''s and other neurodegenerative disorders. Endlyz Therapeutics operates through a model of strong collaboration with academic and research institutions. It has an exclusive partnership with Professor Peter Vangheluwe at KU Leuven and the Centre for Drug Design and Discovery (CD3) to accelerate drug discovery, supported by Quantum AI. The company is backed by a syndicate of investors including SV Health Investors'' DD…', 'https://endlyz.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/endlyztherapeutics/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/2645d60bc6b9d46820de419993219a3e.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/endlyz_therapeutics', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health|Spinout|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2021', '6', 4128786, 'life_sciences'),
('ab98ccd2-a30c-4ac3-a452-d55428650b6c', 'Tenpoint Therapeutics', 'Ophthalmic therapies for aging eye conditions', 'TenPoint Therapeutics is a pioneering startup operating in the healthcare sector, specifically focusing on ocular diseases. The company is at the forefront of a revolution in the treatment of eye diseases, leveraging the potential of regenerative therapies to restore sight. Their approach involves the development of engineered cell-based therapeutics and in vivo reprogramming to reverse vision loss caused by the deterioration of functional tissue in the eye. The company''s unique selling proposition lies in its innovative use of the eye''s properties, which make it an ideal setting for their therapeutic approach. TenPoint Therapeutics employs new techniques to replace lost or damaged cells, potentially restoring their function with a single, long-lasting treatment that reverses the course of disease. The startup''s business model revolves around the development and commercialization of these regenerative therapies. Their target market includes patients suffering from various ocular diseases, with the potential to significantly improve their quality of life. The company was founded by experts from leading institutions in ocular disease, including Moorfields Eye Hospital, UCL Institute of Ophthalmology, Institut de la Vision, and the University of Washington. This gives them a strong foundation in terms of expertise and access to advancements in regenerative biology technologies. In terms of revenue generation, it can be inferred that the company aims to make money by selling the…', 'https://tenpointtherapeutics.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/tenpointtherapeutics/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/04/30/1b393dae7928375d6358787c009d592b.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/tenpoint_therapeutics', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.50262, -0.01321528, 'Life sciences|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Ophthalmology|Eye Diseases|Spinout|Digital Therapeutics|Biotech and Pharma|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2020', '125', 117424195, 'life_sciences'),
('59979ebc-f84f-4252-a644-e0ef79d1c820', 'Vidiia', 'AI-powered platform accelerating diagnostic assay development', 'Vidiia Ltd focuses on expediting the transition of newly researched assays into high-impact, cost-effective, and deployable diagnostic tools. The company was founded by an individual with a background in engineering, specifically in control systems and software for laboratory equipment and scientific instrumentation, who has also served as a director and investor in several early-stage medical device and diagnostic companies. Vidiia collaborates with universities and research institutions to move academic research into practical applications. It utilizes artificial intelligence to improve the speed and accuracy of diagnostic tests. The business model centers on creating affordable diagnostic solutions that can be easily deployed in various healthcare settings, ranging from hospitals and labs to remote clinics. This approach aims to reduce the time and costs associated with traditional diagnostic methods, thereby enhancing healthcare accessibility globally. The company''s services are built on several key pillars: accelerating assay development through partnerships, using AI to refine diagnostics, focusing on cost-effectiveness, and ensuring the diagnostics are deployable in diverse environments. By concentrating on these areas, Vidiia aims to address the needs of different healthcare settings and improve patient care and public health outcomes. Keywords: diagnostic development, AI diagnostics, assay acceleration, deployable diagnostics, medical technology, healthcare solution…', 'https://vidiia.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/vidiia-ltd/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/cc23d1a0272fdb125a7459fb8a6a9b65.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/vidiia', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.5147, -0.1235711, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Health|Patient Care|Health Diagnostics|Spinout|Digital Care|remote health monitoring|DT and LS|rio engineering biology|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2020', '7', 239788, 'life_sciences'),
('1d2cbba8-4cb8-4587-aedb-335de64a73c4', 'Hilltop Leaf', 'Pharmaceutical-grade medicinal cannabis products for specialist prescription', 'Hilltop Leaf, a private medicinal cannabis cultivation and extraction company, was established in 2019 with a focus on supplying the UK and European markets. The company was founded by a team with diverse expertise: Hamish Clegg, a former financier with experience in healthcare and financial markets; Neil Ewart, a Chartered Surveyor with a background in farm management and wind farm projects; and Will Ewart, who brings agricultural experience as a managing partner of a sheep and cattle farm. Their collective backgrounds in finance, agriculture, and renewable energy underpin the company''s strategy. The company is positioning itself to address a key vulnerability in the UK''s medicinal cannabis market: a heavy reliance on imports. By establishing a domestic production facility, Hilltop Leaf aims to provide a reliable and affordable supply of pharmaceutical-grade, cannabis-based products for medicinal use in humans (CBPMs). The business operates as a cultivator and extractor, with plans to produce cannabinoid oils and Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients (API). Its business model revolves around the cultivation of cannabis to GAcP standards and processing to EU GMP standards within a secure facility in Southern Scotland. Revenue is generated through the sale of these products to the specialist prescription market, targeting a significant share of the UK market. By January 2025, the company had already become an operational wholesaler, posting over £3 million in sales of CBPM medici…', 'https://hilltopleaf.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/hilltop-leaf/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/424d242e95f09af1a16dc5f84c4beede.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/hilltop_leaf_limited', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.514412, -0.13092852, 'Life sciences|Pharmaceutical|Health|Biotechnology|Hard Tech|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2020', '16', 4929569, 'life_sciences'),
('05ef990e-33c6-443d-bd0a-d9bbd0982890', 'Sequential Skin', 'Microbiome testing and biomarker analysis for personal care.', 'Sequential Skin operates as a B2B biotechnology company providing an end-to-end platform for clinical testing and analysis in the personal care, and pharmaceutical industries. The company was co-founded by Dr. Oliver Worsley (CEO) and Dr. Albert Dashi (CSO), who both hold PhDs from the Genome Institute of Singapore. Their collective expertise in molecular genetics, microbiome research, and molecular science underpins the company''s scientific approach. The firm''s core business involves providing in-vivo testing services for skincare, scalp care, oral care, and intimate care products to substantiate product claims and guide development. Its proprietary platform manages the entire research process, from study design and participant recruitment to laboratory analysis and data interpretation. Sequential Skin specializes in measuring how ingredients and formulations affect the human microbiome and other molecular biomarkers, turning complex biological data into actionable insights for its clients. The company utilizes next-generation gene-sequencing technology and deep molecular analysis to evaluate the impact of products. This enables clients, which include major skincare and healthcare companies, to develop scientifically validated products. The company''s business model is centered on providing these testing and data analysis services to other businesses, helping them to create effective and credible products. A significant asset is its large clinical dataset, comprising over 50…', 'https://sequential.bio', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/sequentialbio/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/0078616366340b55aace64bed97171ac.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/sequential_skin', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.51866, -0.14232793, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health Platform|Personal Health|Testing|Health|Health and Wellness|Dermatology|Microbiome|Biotech and Pharma|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2020', '25', 5720344, 'life_sciences'),
('23e676fa-fbd4-4951-944b-cb075a39b6f4', 'Tewke', 'AI-driven home automation platform enhancing energy efficiency, security, and personalized comfort', 'Tewke operates in the home automation market, offering a platform that integrates advanced security systems and health-focused technologies to create a personalized living environment. The business model revolves around AI-enabled automation that learns from user routines to optimize energy efficiency, reduce environmental impact, and enhance home comfort. Tewke serves homeowners seeking to improve their living spaces through smart technology, providing solutions that adapt to individual schedules and weather conditions. Revenue is generated through the sale of its automation platform and related services, targeting consumers interested in sustainable and secure home management. The company emphasizes data privacy and security, ensuring that user information is handled with care. Tewke''s platform not only monitors home conditions but also provides actionable insights to users, promoting eco-friendly habits and cost savings. Keywords: home automation, AI, energy efficiency, security, personalized comfort, smart technology, sustainable living, data privacy, eco-friendly, cost savings.', 'https://tewke.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/tewke/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/743776d7544480385dc2cf234c85102c.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/tewke', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.503487, -0.0781497, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Health Platform|Health|Smart Home|B Corp|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2020', '22', 4100000, 'life_sciences'),
('97d52157-0ce1-47f6-8e60-bfa133b721d7', 'CheMastery', 'Robotic automation platform for chemical research and manufacturing', 'CheMastery is a London-based company developing an automation platform to standardize and streamline chemical research and manufacturing. Founded by CEO Dr. Anna Andreou and CTO Dr. Stefan Glatzel, the company aims to address fundamental inefficiencies in the chemical industry, where a significant portion of a chemist''s time is spent on repetitive, manual tasks. This manual process often leads to issues with reproducibility, increased costs, and slower innovation. Dr. Andreou, a chemical methodologist with a PhD from the University of Cambridge, brings over a decade of laboratory and commercialization experience, while Dr. Glatzel holds a PhD in Material Science and has over 20 years of experience in building hardware and software technologies. The company''s core offering is a robotic platform capable of automating approximately 90% of organic chemistry processes, from synthesis and purification to analysis. This allows for 24/7 laboratory operations, freeing chemists to focus on higher-value activities like innovation and strategic planning. CheMastery targets small to medium-scale chemical production across various sectors, including pharmaceuticals, biotechnology, materials science, food, and cosmetics. The business model includes a flexible "Robot as a Service" option, making advanced automation accessible to businesses of different sizes. In December 2022, CheMastery announced an oversubscribed multi-million-pound seed funding round led by Science Angel Syndicate and Un…', 'https://chemastery.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/chemastery/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/44c8e8576cb03b28df5679f2f1a2acb8.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/chemastery', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.489334, -0.14405508, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|Autonomous & Sensor Tech|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Drug Development|Chemistry|Tech for Biotech and Pharma|Woman Founder|DT and LS|rio engineering biology|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2019', '11', 1000000, 'life_sciences'),
('ef8449d0-f1db-4c8c-b3b8-300ebb486ff3', 'Five Lives', 'Mobile app for dementia risk reduction', 'Five Lives, founded in 2019 by Xavier Louis and Sylvain Piquet, is a digital therapeutics company with headquarters in London and Tours, France, that developed a mobile application to assess and reduce the risk of dementia. The founders, who both came from families with medical backgrounds and had extensive experience in the tech industry, including at the brain training app Peak, were motivated to create a purposeful company to address dementia prevention. The direct-to-consumer app, also available for B2B partnerships, is designed to detect and lower the chances of developing dementia by managing five key lifestyle areas: nutrition, sleep, physical activity, mood, and mental stimulation. Users begin with a risk assessment based on a machine learning algorithm, which was trained on data from over 300,000 individuals in the UK Biobank study. This assessment provides a 10-year risk horizon for developing dementia. Based on the results, the app provides personalized coaching, educational content, brain games, and activities like music therapy to help users adopt healthier habits. For high-risk individuals, the app recommends a consultation with a doctor. The company operates on a subscription-based model, offering a free trial before users pay an annual fee for full access to the app''s features. In November 2022, Five Lives raised €3.7 million in a seed round led by Headline and Speedinvest to fund clinical validation and expand its user base in the UK, Australia, France, and …', 'https://fivelives.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/fivelives/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/931b5969beed7246753d2e4233a5ae7e.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/sharptx', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.53256, -0.12221395, 'Life sciences|Mobile app|Health Platform|Health|Cognitive|Mental Health|Alzheimers Disease|Degenerative Diseases|Digital Therapeutics|Tech for Patients|Silver Economy|EIT Health|EIT Ecosystem|elderly care|Horizon Europe|Digital Care|Preventive Care|observatoire healthtech', '2019', '20', 4699998, 'life_sciences'),
('cd1881d4-29da-4c0f-82f3-0286ef490ce9', 'IMU Biosciences', 'AI immune-profiling platform CytAtlas for precision medicine', 'IMU Biosciences is a UK biotechnology company founded in 2021 by Dr Adam Laing, Dr Tom Hayday and Mario Cantero that builds CytAtlas, an AI-powered systems immune-profiling platform rooted in research from King’s College London and the Francis Crick Institute. From a small blood sample CytAtlas analyses vast immune datasets to quantify thousands of cell subsets for applications in immuno-oncology, cell therapy, autoimmune disease and transplantation, and IMU participates in the UK MANIFEST cancer-immunotherapy consortium. After an earlier £11.5 million Series A tranche in January 2024 led by Molten Ventures, in June 2026 IMU announced an oversubscribed financing that brought its Series A to over $53 million (about £40 million), co-led by IQ Capital and Molten Ventures with the British Business Bank, Meltwind and existing investors, taking total funding to about $60 million to expand operations, clinical-platform infrastructure and programs in transplantation and cancer immunotherapy. Sources: company/British Business Bank Jun 2026; Fierce Biotech; BioXconomy.', 'https://imubiosciences.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/imubiosciences/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/09/27/8d7e60ec5f1b804a46035841ef6010f5.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/imu_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.50262, -0.01321528, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Machine Learning|BioTechnology|Health Platform|Health|Oncology|Core AI|Precision Medicine|Immune System|Cell Therapy|Hard Tech|Woman Founder|Longevity|AI Applications|Digital Pharma|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2019', '85', 51500000, 'life_sciences'),
('b550a852-2893-45de-be3b-43b5d7392dde', 'Epoch Biodesign', 'Designing and scaling the first enzymes capable of transforming plastics into low-carbon, circular chemicals', 'Epoch Biodesign is a London deep-tech company that designs AI-discovered enzymes to break down and recycle plastics and textiles, including nylon 6,6, into circular chemicals at commercial scale. In March 2026 it closed a $12 million / about €10.3 million strategic funding round with lululemon, KOMPAS VC, Happiness Capital, Extantia, Leitmotif and others, bringing total capital raised to over $50 million to commercialise enzymatic nylon recycling and build a London demonstration facility (following an earlier Series A). Sources: Tech.eu 25 March 2026; EU-Startups; TechCrunch.', 'https://epochbiodesign.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/epochbiodesign/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/04/30/4b7c457fc2c43d4274e08dd11837c15a.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/epoch_biodesign_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.52141, -0.0873458, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Recycling|Health|Synthetic Biology|Sustainable Development Goals|Advanced Materials|Climate Tech|Circular Economy|BIA Techbio UK|Techbio|Techbio Drug Discovery|AI Material Discovery|Digital Pharma|DT and LS|uk rio|rio engineering biology|rio Synbio in Life Sciences|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Chemicals', '2019', '86', 33453690, 'life_sciences'),
('3e2760d7-a9b8-4e0f-84bc-46bfd300b9f8', 'iLoF', 'AI and photonics platform for personalized drug discovery.', 'iLoF, short for Intelligent Lab on Fiber, is a digital health company that has developed a platform using artificial intelligence and photonics to accelerate personalized drug discovery and development. Founded in 2019 by Luis Valente (CEO), Dr. Mehak Mumtaz (COO), Joana Paiva (CTO), and Professor Paula Sampaio (CSO), the company has dual headquarters in Porto, Portugal, and Oxford, UK. The founding team combines expertise in computer science, business strategy, personalized medicine, and biomedical sciences. The core technology originated from the Ph.D. project of co-founder Joana Paiva. The company''s platform works by analyzing light-based signals from small, non-invasively collected biological samples like blood to create unique biological profiles, or "optical fingerprints". These fingerprints are stored in a cloud-based digital library and analyzed by AI algorithms to identify disease biomarkers and stratify patient populations. This process helps pharmaceutical and biotech companies make clinical trials for complex, heterogeneous diseases like Alzheimer''s more efficient and patient-centric. iLoF states its technology can reduce the costs of clinical trial screening by 40% and the time spent by 70%. The business model is B2B, focusing on partnerships and providing a service subscription for access to its data. iLoF has raised a total of over $8 million through a combination of equity funding and grants. A significant seed round in 2022 raised $5 million, which included …', 'https://ilof.tech', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/iloftech/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/09/27/ecfbc6e1a0b306f9e91475fdcb9bfd43.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/ilof', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.526615, -0.0883325, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Big Data|Deep Tech|Deep Learning|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health Platform|Personal Health|Health|Oncology|Drug Development|Alzheimers Disease|Screening|Core AI|Precision Medicine|Health Diagnostics|Spinout|Sustainable Development Goals|EIC|Wild Card (EIT Health)|Wild Card 2019 (EIT Health)|Tech for Biotech and Pharma|EIT Health|Photonics Tech|AI Drug Discovery|Techbio|EIT Supernovas|CompBio|Woman Founder|EIT Ecosystem|Techbio Drug Discovery|Seal of Excellence EC|AI Applications|Horizon Europe|Digital Pharma|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF biotech|slush24|slush23|slush22|NIF Crisis preparedness|DT and LS|4YFN 2024|4YFN 2022|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|4YFN|comp bio and chem|science-based', '2019', '42', 9824767, 'life_sciences'),
('3f813dd0-05c4-4eaf-8e1d-b6c3944967d8', 'CoMind', 'Non-invasive neuro-monitoring devices to enable bedside access to previously inaccessible brain signals', 'CoMind is a pioneering company in the field of neurotechnology, focusing on the development of advanced neuromonitoring devices and neural interfaces. These technologies aim to revolutionize patient care by providing doctors with access to a wide range of critical neurophysiological signals that are currently difficult to measure. The company serves healthcare providers, particularly those specializing in neurology and brain disorders, by offering non-invasive solutions that optimize patient outcomes across the care continuum. Operating in the healthcare and medical devices market, CoMind employs a business model centered around the research, development, and commercialization of its innovative products. Revenue is generated through the sale of these neuromonitoring devices to hospitals, clinics, and research institutions globally. The company also collaborates with medical professionals and institutions to ensure the practical application and continuous improvement of its technologies. CoMind''s team comprises experts in non-invasive neuroimaging, neuroscience, and biomedical engineering, all committed to advancing the field of neurotechnology. The company is dedicated to fostering an inclusive environment that promotes collaboration and idea sharing across multiple disciplines, driving innovation and impactful product development. Keywords: neurotechnology, neuromonitoring, neural interfaces, non-invasive, neurophysiological signals, patient care, healthcare, medical device…', 'https://comind.io', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/comindtechnologies/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/02/05/d5dc9194929e47fd74ae9617be762149.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/comind_2', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.522564, -0.1086453, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Hardware|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Health|Biomarkers|Neurology|Core AI|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Health Diagnostics|Wearable|Clinical Decision Support|Future of Computing|Brain Computer Interfaces|Optical Sensors|Brain Health|Woman Founder|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF biotech|NIF Crisis preparedness|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI medical devices|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2018', '92', 73409065, 'life_sciences'),
('036aebed-760a-45b7-a353-3e45a3439b03', 'Ecopoint Medical', 'Fibre optic sensors for cardiovascular diagnostics', 'Echopoint Medical is a medical device company, spun out from University College London (UCL) in 2018, that is developing solutions for cardiovascular diagnostics. The company was founded by a multidisciplinary team of engineers and clinicians: Professor Adrien Desjardins, Dr. Richard Colchester, Professor Ioannis Papakonstantinou, and Dr. Malcolm Finlay, a Consultant Cardiologist at Barts Heart Centre. The founders'' journey began with research at UCL, exploring how to integrate fibre optic sensors into minimally invasive devices to provide new sensing and imaging capabilities inside the human body. The company''s flagship product is the iKOr™ microcatheter system. This device uses a thin catheter with a 0.2mm wide fibre optic sensor that measures temperature and pressure to assess blood flow and detect obstructions in coronary arteries. It is specifically designed to address a diagnostic gap in conditions like Ischemia and No Obstructive Coronary Artery Disease (INOCA), which disproportionately affects women and involves problems with the heart''s smallest blood vessels (microvasculature) that are difficult to see in standard angiograms. By providing a complete physiological profile of the heart''s vessels in real-time, the iKOr system aims to give clinicians more precise data to guide treatment decisions, potentially reducing unnecessary stent procedures and improving outcomes for patients who could be treated with medication. Echopoint Medical operates in the medical technolo…', 'https://echopointmedical.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/echopoint-medical-ltd/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/da77ca9f6158e1eb7514a60a5bfad4f7.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/ecopoint_medical', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.519318, -0.1401046, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|IoT InternetOfThings|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Testing|Health|Spinout|Hard Tech|medical testing|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2018', '17', 8889999, 'life_sciences'),
('a5110990-1b9f-4d48-92ee-2b75d6cf9a55', 'MiiCare', 'AI that is helping carers to deliver outstanding care at home', 'MiiCare is a technology-driven company focused on empowering older adults to live independently and safely in their own homes. The company operates in the elder care market, providing AI-driven solutions that include real-time monitoring and predictive analytics to prevent accidents and health issues. MiiCare primarily serves older adults and their families, as well as healthcare providers and local authorities. The business model revolves around offering subscription-based services and partnerships with healthcare organizations. Revenue is generated through these subscriptions and collaborations, ensuring a steady income stream while delivering value to its clients. Keywords: AI, elderly care, independence, safety, real-time monitoring, predictive analytics, healthcare, subscription-based, partnerships, innovation.', 'https://miicare.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/miicare/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/29/3c5893eb4d767e692d64596527c2dad1.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/miicare', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.520756, -0.1219118, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Health Platform|Health|Remote Monitoring|Patient Care|Core AI|Direct-to-Consumer|European Health Catapult (EIT Health)|European Health Catapult 2020 (EIT Health)|Tech for Patients|Silver Economy|EIT Health|Hard Tech|EIT Ecosystem|AI Applications|elderly care|Horizon Europe|Digital Care|remote health monitoring|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2018', '20', 5913667, 'life_sciences'),
('6633f395-43a3-4f45-b067-e31df6fb48bd', 'ZOE', 'AI-powered personalized nutrition program using at-home testing', 'ZOE is a health science company that provides a personalized nutrition program based on scientific research and artificial intelligence. Co-founded in 2017 by Tim Spector, Jonathan Wolf, and George Hadjigeorgiou, the company''s mission is to improve long-term health by helping individuals understand their unique biological responses to food. The concept originated from Spector''s research on twins, which demonstrated that even genetically identical individuals have different metabolic responses to the same foods, largely due to their unique gut microbiomes. Spector, a professor of genetic epidemiology, had a personal health scare that motivated him to create ZOE. He partnered with Jonathan Wolf, who has a background in physics and technology, and George Hadjigeorgiou, an entrepreneur who founded and sold a large online food delivery company. Wolf''s experience is in machine learning, while Hadjigeorgiou''s came from a personal interest in nutrition after discovering he had high cholesterol. The trio launched ZOE after securing initial funding to conduct the world''s largest nutrition science study, known as the PREDICT studies, in collaboration with institutions like King''s College London, Harvard, and Stanford. The company''s direct-to-consumer business model begins with customers purchasing an at-home test kit. This kit includes a stool sample test for gut microbiome analysis, a blood fat test, and a continuous glucose monitor (CGM) worn for two weeks to measure blood sugar resp…', 'https://zoe.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/joinzoe/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/22/36929249c92353762ab56a1827511a20.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/zoe', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.498917, -0.11568895, 'Life sciences|Virtual Reality|BioTechnology|Health Platform|Innovative Food|Testing|Health|Weight Management|Nutrition|Microbiome|Spinout|Metabolism|Sustainable Development Goals|Tech for Patients|Hard Tech|Food as Medicine|Digital Care|medical testing|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based|Food', '2017', '424', 80578758, 'life_sciences'),
('0e688afb-0e95-4a77-a5bb-f720b0b1e3be', 'Valkyrie Industries', 'Valkyrie enables an augmented & realistic sensation of touch in a virtual world', 'Valkyrie Industries, founded in London in 2017 by Kourosh Atefipour, Dr. Ivan Isakov, and Oliver Cleveley-Jones, is a technology firm specializing in haptic solutions for virtual reality (VR) and neuromuscular recovery. The company has developed a patented Neuromuscular Electrical Muscle Stimulation (NMES) wearable technology designed to allow users to feel and interact with digital environments. The founders'' backgrounds are integral to the company''s direction. CEO Kourosh Atefipour holds MA and MSc degrees in Innovation Design Engineering from the Royal College of Art and Imperial College London. His experience in industrial design with brands like Nokia and McLaren informs the company''s product development and market strategy. CTO Dr. Ivan Isakov has a Ph.D. in nanotechnology from UCL and a background in physics, which underpins the scientific development of their hardware. His work focuses on human-computer interfaces and embodied control in VR. The duo''s journey began at an Imperial College incubator, where they identified the sense of touch as a missing link in immersive experiences. Valkyrie Industries initially targeted industrial and professional applications, such as training for dangerous or complex jobs, where haptic feedback could add significant value. Their early prototypes, sometimes referred to as the "Iron Man" suit, used electrical impulses to simulate muscle resistance and touch. Over time, the company has pivoted to focus on the fitness and healthcare ma…', 'https://valkyrie-vr.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/valkyrieindustries/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/28/9bc43517f8c4f2d3d505a068c6ff6b73.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/valkyrie_industries', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|Augmented Reality|Virtual Reality|Connected Device|IoT InternetOfThings|Medical Devices|Health|Sports|Patient Care|Immersive Technologies|Wearable|Hard Tech|Digital Care|remote health monitoring|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2017', '9', 1066197, 'life_sciences'),
('e7f05203-8f2f-4abf-9f4a-b9326840d0cb', 'Oxford Medical Simulation', 'Delivers virtual reality medical simulation - training healthcare professionals to provide consistently world-class patient management without risking lives', 'Oxford Medical Simulation (OMS) specializes in providing immersive virtual reality (VR) simulations for healthcare training. The company serves a diverse range of clients including medical schools, nursing programs, and healthcare institutions. Operating in the healthcare education market, OMS aims to enhance the skills and preparedness of medical professionals by offering realistic and accessible training experiences. The business model is primarily subscription-based, allowing institutions to access a library of VR scenarios for a recurring fee. Revenue is generated through these subscriptions as well as through one-time purchases of specific training modules. OMS''s innovative approach ensures that healthcare professionals can practice and refine their skills in a safe, controlled environment before encountering real-life medical situations. Keywords: VR simulations, healthcare training, medical education, immersive learning, nursing programs, medical schools, subscription model, skill enhancement, preparedness, virtual reality.', 'https://oxfordmedicalsimulation.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/oxfordmedicalsimulation/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/877922dae1aed0b039a9a3cfe593cc37.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/oxford_medical_simulation', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.501896, -0.0922925, 'Life sciences|Virtual Reality|Health Platform|Learning Tools and Resources|Health|Surgery|Medical Education|Medical Training|Immersive Technologies|Surgical Equipment|Corporate Learning|Physician Support Tools|Hard Tech|Health It|Education', '2017', '118', 16643933, 'life_sciences'),
('c0f9f9a2-bc17-4540-9df3-a98e45f08e48', 'Automata', 'Robotic automation platform for life science laboratories', 'Automata Technologies is a London-based company founded in 2015 by architects Mostafa ElSayed and Suryansh Chandra, who met while working at Zaha Hadid Architects. Their experience with computational design and robotics in architecture revealed the complexity and limitations of modern automation, inspiring them to establish a company aimed at making automation more accessible across various industries. Initially, the company explored applications in manufacturing, but soon narrowed its focus to the life sciences sector, where they identified a significant opportunity to transform laboratory operations. Automata develops and provides the LINQ platform, a vertically integrated lab automation solution designed for the life sciences market. This platform combines modular robotic hardware, cloud-based software, and a robust data infrastructure to automate laboratory workflows. The core hardware component is the LINQ Bench, a configurable robotic bench that can be customized to fit various lab spaces and integrate with over 800,000 different instrument configurations. The system utilizes robotic arms and transport options like the Bridge and Maglev to move samples between instruments, enabling end-to-end workflow automation with minimal human intervention. This allows for "walkaway time," freeing up scientists to focus on data analysis and experimental design rather than manual, repetitive tasks. The company''s business model centers on providing these automation solutions to a ran…', 'https://automata.tech', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/automata-technologies/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/ef02f12a29a5bbea9a9bf9d0dc7cbbf8.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/automata', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.530655, -0.1124089, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Hardware|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Health Platform|Supply Chain Management|Industrial Automation|Health|Core AI|Industrial Robotics|Medical Robots|Industrial Technology|Manufacturing and Assembly Robots|Manufacturing Tech|Manufacturing|AI Drug Discovery|BIA Techbio UK|Techbio|Hard Tech|Techbio Drug Discovery|Lab Automation|AI Applications|Digital Pharma|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF biotech|NIF Crisis preparedness|DT and LS|rio ai health|rio AI health life sciences|uk rio|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Robotics', '2015', '167', 101413597, 'life_sciences'),
('ad45dfae-0c5d-4e63-a29c-0f8dc2da7307', 'Curileum Discovery', 'Novel therapeutics correcting cell production in gut mucosa', 'Curileum Discovery is a London-based biotechnology company founded by Dr. Jeff Moore in 2013, focusing on early intervention in the development of serious gastrointestinal (GI) diseases. The firm''s scientific approach is based on identifying defective stem cells in intestinal mucosal biopsies and developing novel therapeutics to correct cell production in the gut''s regenerating mucosal barrier. Curileum has developed a small molecule, ULI-015, to reduce polyp formation and its progression to bowel cancer, and a stem cell therapy, ATZ, to repair fistulising conditions in Crohn''s disease patients. The company''s strategy involves discovering and validating new therapeutic targets and then partnering with pharmaceutical companies for further drug development and commercialization. The business model is centered on licensing these preclinical candidates to major pharma companies, with potential terms including upfront payments and future milestone payments on marketed therapies. Dr. Jeff Moore, the Founder and CEO, has a career focused on regulating cell production in highly regenerative tissues like bone marrow and the intestinal mucosa. His background includes research at the US National Institutes of Health (NIH), the Walter and Elisa Hall Institute (WEHI) in Melbourne, DNAX Research Institute in Palo Alto, and ImClone Systems in New York. He previously founded Phylogix Inc, securing $15 million in venture capital funding, and led a regenerative medicine collaboration with Nov…', 'https://curileum.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/curileum-discovery-ltd/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/11/20/de7b0e72f87ea366b781b9fce7dc589d.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/curileum_discovery', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.57849, -0.3176997, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health|Oncology|Biotech and Pharma|Hard Tech|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2013', '3', 3193999, 'life_sciences'),
('4013ce41-8989-4450-84ee-a4df4321a066', 'LabGenius', 'Combining human and machine intelligence to accelerate the discovery of advanced medicines', 'LabGenius is a pioneering startup in the drug discovery sector, leveraging advanced technologies like machine learning (ML), synthetic biology, and laboratory automation to develop next-generation protein therapeutics. The company operates in the biopharmaceutical market, focusing on creating innovative treatments for various diseases, including inflammatory conditions. LabGenius primarily serves pharmaceutical companies and biotech firms looking to enhance their drug discovery processes. By integrating ML-driven protein engineering, LabGenius optimizes therapeutic nanobodies—small antibody fragments that can be used to treat diseases. This approach allows for more efficient and targeted drug development, potentially reducing the time and cost associated with bringing new drugs to market. The business model of LabGenius revolves around collaborations and partnerships with major pharmaceutical companies. For instance, their collaboration with Ablynx, a Sanofi company, showcases their ability to apply their ML-driven platform to real-world drug discovery challenges. These partnerships not only validate LabGenius''s technology but also provide a revenue stream through research and development agreements, milestone payments, and potential royalties from successful drug candidates. LabGenius makes money by offering its cutting-edge platform as a service to pharmaceutical companies. They charge for access to their technology and expertise, and they may also receive payments based o…', 'https://labgeni.us', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/labgenius/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/53c56c63eca57d0ae91b315fc7a0e01a.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/labgenius', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.494064, -0.0631783, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Hardware|Deep Tech|BioTechnology|Health|Oncology|Drug Development|DNA|Genetics and genomics|Core AI|Synthetic Biology|Tech for Biotech and Pharma|AI Drug Discovery|BIA Techbio UK|Techbio|CompBio|Techbio Drug Discovery|AI Applications|Digital Pharma|NIF defense security and resilience|NIF biotech|NIF Crisis preparedness|proteomics|DT and LS|uk rio|rio engineering biology|rio Synbio in Life Sciences|UKis Digital and technologies|uk is8 digital and technologies|uk is8 life sciences|comp bio and chem|science-based', '2012', '66', 57892112, 'life_sciences')
