('1ef73b78-bc97-4427-a089-0e4e82360485', 'Qured', 'Health screening designed for every employee', 'Qured is on a mission to start a million people on a lifelong preventative healthcare journey. Today, we do this with a whole-workforce health screening programme with clinical wrap around. We help enterprises with large front-line workforces keep their people well and productive at work through targeting the major physical drivers of long-term absence - which the programme can reduce by 20% or more. It''s affordable and delivers outsized impact through amazing uptake - over 80% even in hard to reach populations.', 'https://qured.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/qured/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/16/86cb74b4e82475dab75652135e1a80c6.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/qured', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.52195, -0.08488, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Mobile app|Health Platform|Personal Health|Corporate Wellness|Health|Home Healthcare|Health and Wellness|Telemedicine|Screening|Health Diagnostics|Sustainable Development Goals|Woman Founder|Health It|Preventive Care|rio ai health|uk is8 digital and technologies|Enterprise Software', '2024', '33', 1720000, 'life_sciences'),
('a8a26a76-08a7-4724-af47-253e6975ed87', 'SPARTA Biodiscovery', 'Automated single nanoparticle analysis for next-generation therapeutics', 'SPARTA Biodiscovery is a spin-out from Imperial College London, founded in 2022 by Professor Dame Molly Stevens and Dr. Jelle Penders, to commercialize a novel nanoparticle analysis platform. The company''s creation was a direct result of years of research within the Stevens Group at the university, addressing a pressing need for more advanced analytical tools in the development of next-generation pharmaceuticals. Dr. Penders, who serves as the CEO, co-invented the core technology and spearheaded its technical development during his time as a researcher, drawing on his background in biomaterials, analytical chemistry, and nano-characterization. Professor Stevens, a globally recognized researcher in biomedical materials and a serial entrepreneur, serves as co-founder and advisory board chair. The firm’s core offering is the SPARTA® (Single Particle Automated Raman Trapping Analysis) technology, a benchtop instrument that provides high-throughput, label-free chemical analysis of individual nanoparticles. This platform overcomes the limitations of traditional bulk analysis methods, which typically only measure average characteristics, by delivering detailed physico-chemical data on a single-particle basis. The technology uses a laser to trap and analyze each particle, generating a chemical fingerprint that reveals its size, composition, drug loading, and stability. This capability is crucial for clients in the pharmaceutical and biotechnology sectors, enabling them to accelerate…', 'https://spartabiodiscovery.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/sparta-biodiscovery/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/04/36326834119f2faa923c43d6f375043d.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/sparta_biodiscovery', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.558575, 0.1476176, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health|Spinout|Hard Tech|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2022', '23', 4225000, 'life_sciences'),
('440fab81-df43-49dd-9c16-c5bf4466957e', 'Panda Surgical', 'Handheld robotic platform enhancing minimally invasive neurosurgery', 'Panda Surgical Limited is a University College London (UCL) spinout company founded in 2022 by Manios Dimitrakakis (CEO), UCLH neurosurgeon Hani Marcus (CMO), and UCL Professor Danail Stoyanov (Scientific Advisor). The company was established to translate the technology developed during Dimitrakakis''s PhD in handheld robotic devices for neurosurgery into a clinical product. The founding team combines expertise in robotics engineering and clinical neurosurgery, with Professor Stoyanov having prior experience with a med-tech exit to Olympus and an affiliation with Medtronic, and Mr. Marcus being a consultant neurosurgeon specializing in pituitary and skull base tumors. The company is developing a next-generation handheld robotics platform to improve the efficacy and safety of minimally invasive neurosurgery. This system provides surgeons with enhanced dexterity, control, and decision support for operating in confined spaces deep within the brain and spine. The platform features a reusable, lightweight, motorized handle controller that connects to a series of interchangeable, single-use wristed surgical tools—such as graspers, scissors, and dissectors—that are only 3mm in diameter. This design allows for delicate maneuvers, motion scaling, and tremor filtration at a fraction of the cost of larger robotic systems. The business model addresses the challenges surgeons face with conventional instruments in minimally invasive procedures, which can limit access and increase the risk …', 'https://panda-surgical.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/panda-surgical/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2024/12/18/da01e66ba914e086dad0ae0f49035b50.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/panda_surgical', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.546497, -0.0226905, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Health|Surgery|Neurology|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|Spinout|Surgical Robots|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based|Robotics', '2022', '14', 2983718, 'life_sciences'),
('30509ed4-6973-4569-aff9-ac37faebe858', 'The OVA', 'Reproductive health supplements for egg and sperm vitality', 'The OVA Co is a UK-based manufacturer of reproductive health supplements designed to support individuals and couples through every stage of their fertility journey, from pre-conception to postpartum. The company was founded by Danielle Fox-Thomas and Kat Lestage, two former Net-A-Porter executives who drew upon their personal experiences with IVF and recurrent miscarriage to address a gap in the market for transparent, science-backed, and empathetic fertility support. Their mission is to deliver high-quality, effective, and accessible formulas without high mark-ups. The business operates on a direct-to-consumer and retail model, selling its products online via its website and through major retailers like Boots and Sainsbury''s. The product line includes supplements such as OVAHer for fertility and pregnancy support, OVAHim for sperm health, OVAPlus for hormonal support, and OVAOmega, a vegan Omega-3 supplement. These formulations are developed in collaboration with a network of fertility specialists, nutritionists, and biochemists, using bioavailable ingredients in therapeutic dosages to maximize efficacy. The products are manufactured in the UK in FDA-approved facilities and are B-Corp certified. Launched in late 2024 or early 2025, The OVA Co quickly secured over $1 million in a pre-seed funding round led by consumer venture capital firm ERA VC, with participation from Ventures Together and Syndicate Room. This capital is aimed at fueling expansion into Ireland and scaling …', 'https://theovaco.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-ova-co/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/c17ee96a4d5f37365403259550f6f323.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/the_ova', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Dietary Supplements|Fertility|Health|Pregnancy|B Corp|Woman Founder', '2021', '5', 1450140, 'life_sciences'),
('c80d8c9e-16ce-47d3-a261-1d9dedfd6ac0', 'Naturecan', 'Offers the highest quality CBD products on the market', null, 'https://naturecan.gr', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/naturecan-ltd/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/209f7bd52a6a88ed5528f9a0de530ddd.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/naturecan_1_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.493065, -0.21744, 'Life sciences|Health|Wellness Beauty', '2021', '71', 5474474, 'life_sciences'),
('56a4430a-d732-4682-9b51-95ba23784d67', 'Monk', 'Smart ice bath and cold water therapy app', 'Monk is a health technology company that has developed a smart ice bath and an accompanying cold water therapy application. The company''s mission is to enhance mental, physical, and emotional health through the practice of cold water immersion. The company was founded in 2021 by Laura Fullerton, who serves as the CEO. Fullerton was inspired to create a safer and more accessible way for people to practice at-home cold water therapy after discovering a large online community dedicated to converting chest freezers into makeshift ice baths. The company has secured investments from prominent figures such as former Brewdog CEO James Watt and former world heavyweight boxing champion Anthony Joshua. Monk''s primary product is a smart ice bath designed for both indoor and outdoor use. The unit is a ''plug and plunge'' system that does not require plumbing and uses a standard electrical outlet. It features a self-cleaning function with ozone sanitization, requiring water changes only every two to four months. The accompanying mobile application connects with wearable technology like Oura and Whoop to track health metrics such as sleep quality, heart rate, and HRV, showing the impact of cold exposure over time. The app also provides guided plunge programs, breathwork sessions, and allows users to self-report on mental wellness metrics. Monk targets high-performance individuals, including athletes and executives, and has established a partnership with the luxury Fairmont Hotels chain. Keyw…', 'https://discovermonk.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/discovermonk/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/22/7df0ee36fab35b85125490defc94149a.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/monk_2', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.507446, -0.1277653, 'Life sciences|Health|Wellness Beauty|Health and Wellness|Woman Founder', '2021', '18', 212000, 'life_sciences'),
('bcafa9d1-e087-49a5-afe8-dd1fe75c907d', 'Amber Therapeutics', 'Implantable neuromodulation therapy for mixed urinary incontinence', 'Amber Therapeutics is a medical technology company, spun out from the University of Oxford in 2021, developing bioelectrical therapies for functional disorders. The company was co-founded by CEO Aidan Crawley, Chief Engineer Tim Denison, Stefan De Wachter, and Charles Knowles. Crawley, an entrepreneur with a background in finance and tech, was an Entrepreneur in Residence at Oxford Science Enterprises and sought to tackle a significant, unaddressed medical problem. The founding team combines expertise in medical devices, clinical practice, and translational neuroengineering. The company’s lead product, Amber-UI, is a fully implantable, adaptive neuromodulation therapy developed to treat mixed urinary incontinence (MUI) in women, a condition that includes both stress and urge incontinence. The therapy works by targeting the pudendal nerve, which is crucial for continence control, through a minimally invasive surgical procedure. Amber-UI utilizes a closed-loop system called Picostim-DyNeuMo, which can sense physiological signals and adjust electrical stimulation in real-time, effectively creating a ''synthetic reflex arc'' to restore normal bladder function. This adaptive capability allows the therapy to be personalized to the patient and respond dynamically to different activities, such as coughing or lifting. Amber Therapeutics operates by developing and commercializing these neuromodulation therapies, with an initial focus on gaining regulatory approval in the United States. …', 'https://amber-tx.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/amber-therapeutics/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/10/08/a78e3748420de9a70954b16a52b70810.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/amber_therapeutics', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.52133, -0.20278408, 'Life sciences|Hardware|BioTechnology|Medical Devices|Health|medical implants|Neurology|Neuromodulation and Neurostimulation|Spinout|Urology|Pelvic Health|Hard Tech|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2021', '63', 89022545, 'life_sciences'),
('e80aa1e3-6d47-4dd0-a5a2-046256a18f95', 'Jude', 'Turning bladder weakness into bladder care and incontinence into a conversation', 'Jude is a pioneering startup focused on transforming the conversation around bladder weakness and incontinence. The company offers a range of products designed to improve bladder health and provide discreet, effective solutions for managing leaks. Jude''s product lineup includes biodegradable incontinence pads, ultra-thin liners, and clinically proven bladder strength health supplements. These products are designed to be comfortable, soft, and absorbent, catering to the needs of individuals experiencing bladder weakness. Jude primarily serves women over the age of 50, a demographic often underrepresented in consumer markets. By addressing this gap, Jude is tapping into a significant and growing market. The company operates within the health and wellness sector, specifically targeting bladder care and incontinence management. Jude''s business model is direct-to-consumer (DTC), meaning they sell their products directly to customers through their website, wearejude.com. This model allows them to maintain control over the customer experience and build a strong community around their brand. Jude makes money by selling individual products, offering multipacks for cost savings, and providing trial kits to encourage new customers to try their offerings. Additionally, they have a waitlist for upcoming products, indicating strong demand and customer interest. The company''s commitment to sustainability is evident in their use of biodegradable materials for their pads and liners, making t…', 'https://wearejude.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/wearejude/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/02/04/7657be8651a69e103e172e3e1b1aa407.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/jude_1', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.51453, -0.083503, 'Life sciences|Dietary Supplements|Health|Femtech|Hard Tech|Woman Founder', '2021', '72', 6259924, 'life_sciences'),
('93e621c4-56e8-45a6-9c47-340e6f4dc0ee', 'Cryogenx', 'Portable, on-demand body cooling device for heatstroke', 'Cryogenx is a company focused on designing and manufacturing technology to mitigate the effects of extreme heat on human health. It was founded in 2023 by James Mullins and Ewan Jones. The founders'' backgrounds are in engineering, with James Mullins, the CEO, having studied at the University of Bristol and previously worked at the Bristol Medical School, and Ewan Jones, the CTO, also a University of Bristol alumnus with experience at Airbus. The company''s first product is the CGX1, a portable, on-demand body cooling device intended to revolutionize the treatment of exertional heatstroke. The device is designed to emulate the therapeutic effects of ice water immersion, the current gold standard for heatstroke treatment, but with significantly fewer resources, making it highly portable and usable in any scenario. It functions as a closed-loop system that circulates a small volume of ice and water through a specialized garment worn by the patient, a method known as conductive cooling. The CGX1 is aimed at markets where individuals are at high risk of heatstroke, such as the military, elite sports, and emergency services. By providing life-saving cooling capabilities in a backpack-sized format, Cryogenx aims to address the rising global health crisis caused by increasing temperatures. Keywords: body cooling, heatstroke treatment, medical device, portable cooling, conductive cooling, emergency services, military technology, sports medicine, climate technology, patient safety', 'https://cryogenx.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/cryogenx/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/26/cc2324ae026478be02036309d29bdc4c.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/cryogenx', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.556187, -0.14866807, 'Life sciences|Hardware|Deep Tech|Medical Devices|Health|Sports|Critical medical care|Non-Invasive medical devices and treatments|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based', '2019', '11', 2861617, 'life_sciences'),
('bd266584-5e90-48e3-a716-b3b2ffc61511', 'Medicus Health', null, 'Medicus.health is a startup that operates in the healthcare technology sector, specifically targeting primary care providers. The company has developed a next-generation clinical system designed to streamline care services and introduce new, efficient ways of working. This system was created in collaboration with NHS clinicians, indicating a strong focus on practicality and usability in a real-world clinical setting. The company''s primary clients are healthcare organizations of all sizes. Medicus aims to alleviate the burdens of heavy workloads, complex patient needs, and rising workforce pressures that healthcare professionals often face. The company achieves this by providing intuitive tools that simplify daily administrative tasks, allowing healthcare providers to focus more on patient care. Medicus.health operates on a business-to-business model, likely generating revenue through the sale or subscription of its clinical system to healthcare organizations. The company also emphasizes its ongoing support for clients, suggesting a continuous relationship that could potentially include regular system updates, maintenance, and customer service. In essence, Medicus.health is a healthcare technology company that provides a clinical system designed to improve efficiency and collaboration in primary care settings. It serves healthcare organizations, helping them to manage their workload and focus on patient care. Keywords: Healthcare Technology, Primary Care, Clinical System, NHS…', 'https://medicus.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/medicushealth/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/a0687d54d65427264e8f946d42f18000.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/medicus_health', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.53496, -0.12176769, 'Life sciences|Health', '2019', '34', 600000, 'life_sciences'),
('eef464fa-e579-4f4a-a95b-fac2586db309', 'Visionable', 'Visionable is the first video collaboration platform designed especially for healthcare teams’ advanced clinical needs', 'Visionable is a pioneering startup in the healthcare technology sector, focused on transforming the way healthcare services are delivered. The company specializes in creating digital solutions that enable virtual hospitals and care systems, breaking down barriers of distance and accessibility. Visionable''s primary clients include healthcare providers, such as hospitals, clinics, and emergency services, as well as social care organizations. These clients benefit from Visionable''s technology to improve patient care, particularly in critical areas like stroke treatment and emergency response. Operating in the global healthcare market, Visionable leverages its expertise to address the growing demand for connected healthcare solutions. The company''s platform allows medical professionals to collaborate in real-time, regardless of their physical location. This capability is crucial for improving response times and outcomes in emergency situations, as evidenced by their success in reducing the "door to needle" time for stroke patients from 32 minutes to 23 minutes. Visionable''s business model is based on a subscription service, where healthcare institutions pay for access to their platform and its various features. This model ensures a steady stream of revenue while allowing clients to scale their usage based on their needs. Additionally, Visionable offers customized solutions and consulting services to help organizations integrate their technology seamlessly into existing systems. …', 'https://visionable.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/visionable-global', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/fd382b7b761e5607db29a1376d3c2bbb.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/visionable', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.49609, -0.1281522, 'Life sciences|Health Platform|Health|Medical Education|Critical medical care|Telemedicine|Tech for Hospitals and Clinics|Tech for Medical Professionals|Physician Support Tools|Hard Tech|Health It|stroke', '2019', '16', 30916661, 'life_sciences'),
('f6250727-e54a-4aae-9ff0-0532faf5a335', 'Myricx Bio', 'Novel antibody-drug conjugate payloads for cancer treatment', 'Myricx Bio is a UK-based biotechnology company specializing in the discovery and development of a new class of selective cytotoxic payloads for antibody-drug conjugates (ADCs). These ADCs are based on inhibitors of the enzyme NMT (N-myristoyltransferase) and are designed to treat various types of cancer. The company operates in the biopharmaceutical market, targeting oncology therapeutics. Myricx Bio serves pharmaceutical companies and research institutions looking for advanced cancer treatment solutions. The business model revolves around research and development, followed by licensing agreements and partnerships with larger pharmaceutical firms to bring their innovations to market. Revenue is generated through these partnerships, licensing deals, and potentially future sales of developed therapies. Keywords: biotechnology, ADCs, NMT inhibitors, cancer treatment, oncology, cytotoxic payloads, drug development, licensing, partnerships, UK-based.', 'https://myricxpharma.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/myricx-bio/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/f8c387d17cd68fe8192e4367b9b9d85a.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/myricx_pharma', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.50262, -0.01321528, 'Life sciences|Pharmaceutical|BioTechnology|Health|Oncology|Precision Medicine|Spinout|Verified Unicorns and $1B Exits|Biotech and Pharma|Antibody-Drug Conjugate|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2019', '36', 124499996, 'life_sciences'),
('347d4d80-c16f-4ef7-9611-e04a6603e5a5', 'Omnos', 'Omnos - The intelligent health system', null, 'https://omnos.me', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/omnos-limited/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2023/03/23/71fb13494c5fca2f93093f836ae36555.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/omnos', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.50732, -0.1276474, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health Platform|Personal Health|Health|Health and Wellness|Biotech and Pharma|Longevity|Digital Care|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences', '2019', '13', 1077194, 'life_sciences'),
('232532fe-98c2-4075-8e2a-2be8825d94ad', 'NovalGen', 'Autoregulation platform for multi-specific immunotherapy development', 'NovalGen is a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company that develops multi-specific immunotherapies for cancer, autoimmune, and other immunological disorders. The company was founded in 2018 by Professor Amit Nathwani and is headquartered in London, United Kingdom, stemming from proprietary innovation from University College London (UCL). Professor Nathwani, who also serves as CEO, is an entrepreneur in cancer research and gene therapy and previously founded Freeline Therapeutics. He recognized the limitations of existing medicine, which drove him to create new approaches for patients with unmet needs. NovalGen''s core technology is a proprietary autoregulation (AR) platform designed to create safer and more effective drugs by integrating self-regulating capabilities into immunotherapies. This technology aims to mitigate toxicity, improve efficacy, and expand the therapeutic index of treatments like T-cell engagers. The business model focuses on advancing its pipeline of therapeutic candidates through clinical trials, facilitated by a network of academic and strategic partners. The company secures funding from institutional investors, including AlbionVC and UCL Technology Fund, to support its research and development. The company''s lead program, NVG-111, is a bispecific antibody T-cell engager that targets the ROR1 antigen on tumor cells, redirecting T-cells to kill cancer cells. It is being evaluated in Phase 1/2 clinical trials for patients with hematological malignancies s…', 'https://novalgen.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/novalgen/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/3189b6528559eb32d510bfc62743ba3c.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/novalgen', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.605476, -0.4262299, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health|Spinout|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010', '2018', '11', 1939999, 'life_sciences'),
('756ad3cf-64e3-45cf-93e1-6b6bb5bba9d6', 'Little Journey', 'Little Journey supports children & their families undergoing healthcare procedures or participating in clinical trials', 'Little Journey is a digital eSupport platform designed to psychologically prepare, support and inform children and families before, during and after healthcare interactions - both those occurring as part of a clinical trial and within routine care. Our mission is to support all children to better health. We believe that, through the provision of engaging, interactive and age-appropriate content, we can improve healthcare experiences and health outcomes for all. The Little Journey smartphone app enables families to access information and support tailored to their child’s age, procedure type and hospital at a time and location convenient to them. Virtual tours using 360-degree images of the actual rooms families will visit explain what will happen and who children will meet during their hospital journey. Relaxation animations and therapeutic/distraction games further help to reduce anxiety and improve experiences. A parent information section includes articles, checklists and hospital guides – all of which can be configured by healthcare organisations via a web portal. We ensure a truly patient-focused user experience by co-creating content, using a continuous feedback loop with children, families and key stakeholders. Little Journey fundamentally believes in the power of familiarisation and desensitization through immersive play to facilitate individual coping strategy development, reducing peri-procedural anxiety and improving healthcare experiences for all.', 'https://littlejourney.health', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/little-journey/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/27/fb5d2cbeab6fac5009b5af01f35db4b2.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/little_journey', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.49887, -0.1156791, 'Life sciences|Mobile app|Health Platform|Psychology|Health|Remote Monitoring|Mental Health|Patient Engagement|Pediatrics|Digital Therapeutics|Clinical Trials|Physician Support Tools|Hard Tech|Woman Founder|Digital Care|Preventive Care|remote health monitoring', '2018', '44', 10148484, 'life_sciences'),
('e04262ec-5a4d-4f93-a876-96905b6fc64a', 'Good Boost', 'Community-delivered therapeutic exercise programs for better health and wellbeing', 'Good Boost operates as a social enterprise focused on health technology, transforming community spaces like public swimming pools into therapeutic centers for individuals with musculoskeletal (MSK) conditions. The company was established as a social enterprise in 2018 after originating from a community health research project in Oxford, England. The concept was developed by CEO Ben Wilkins, whose background includes a Master''s Degree in Musculoskeletal Science from the University of Oxford and another in Osteopathic Medicine from Oxford Brookes University. Wilkins'' motivation stemmed from personal experiences with his mother''s arthritis and his own recovery from a snowboarding accident, which highlighted the scarcity of accessible MSK support. His work with charities and social enterprises further revealed the challenges patients faced in staying active before major surgeries like hip and knee replacements. Good Boost''s core offering is an AI-powered platform that delivers personalized therapeutic exercise programs for both water and land-based rehabilitation. The technology, a Class 1 Medical Device registered with the MHRA, is built on clinical research and is co-designed with stakeholders to ensure it meets user needs. It creates tailored exercise plans that consider individual conditions and goals, allowing for both solo and group sessions. A key feature is its ability to quantify human movement in water, a significant challenge in aquatic therapy, which aids in assessin…', 'https://goodboost.ai', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/good-boost', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/994cacb03dd22ec4931017b20ab5ff67.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/goodboost', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.413094, -0.2110577, 'Life sciences|Artificial Intelligence|Machine Learning|Mobile app|Health Platform|Psychology|Health|Wellness Beauty|Mental Health|Digital Care|uk is8 digital and technologies', '2018', '25', 2698468, 'life_sciences'),
