('b240a75c-725d-4559-9d6b-faf0239ef121', 'Epsilogen', 'Epsilogen is a global leader in the development of immunoglobulin (IgE) antibodies to treat cancer.', 'Epsilogen is a clinical-stage immuno-oncology company established in 2016 as a spin-out from King''s College London. The company was founded by Professor Sophia Karagiannis, a translational cancer immunologist with extensive experience in both academic and biotechnology settings in the USA and UK. Her research group at King''s College London was the first to design, evaluate, and advance anti-tumor Immunoglobulin E (IgE) antibodies from a concept into clinical trials. Epsilogen is focused on developing a new class of antibody therapeutics for cancer treatment, leveraging the unique properties of different antibody isotypes, primarily IgE. The company''s business model is centered on the research, development, and eventual commercialization of these novel antibody-based drugs. Its revenue generation will depend on achieving clinical milestones, potential partnerships with larger pharmaceutical companies, and ultimately, drug sales upon regulatory approval. Epsilogen has successfully raised significant capital to fund its operations, securing a total of $70.3 million over nine funding rounds. Key investors include Novartis Venture Fund, British Patient Capital, Epidarex Capital, 3B Future Health Fund, and ALSA Ventures. Epsilogen''s core technology platform harnesses the natural function of IgE antibodies, which evolved to provide immunological defense against parasites. This functionality is repurposed to target solid tumors, offering benefits such as high potency, better tumor p…', 'https://epsilogen.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/epsilogen-ltd/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2026/10/26/94fcedb2045605346aada2925e2d8885.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/epsilogen', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.540146, -0.1368618, 'Life sciences|BioTechnology|Health|Spinout|Biotech and Pharma|Woman Founder|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|UKSU|UKSU2010|science-based', '2016', '33', 62860001, 'life_sciences'),
('07627a71-0339-484b-bd58-5d3dd8ef550c', 'Fresh Check', 'Visual color-change hygiene verification swab and app', 'Fresh Check Ltd. develops technology to detect bacterial and chemical contamination on surfaces. Founded in London in 2015 by Imperial College London PhD alumni Alex Bond and John Simpson, the company originated from their research into visualizing microbial contamination. The idea was born out of personal frustration with food spoilage and the risks of food poisoning. The company''s core offering is the FreshCheck Hygiene Verification System, which consists of a patented color-changing swab and a digital application available on Android and iOS. This system provides a visual, qualitative result in under 30 seconds, indicating whether a surface is clean or contaminated without requiring an expensive reader. The technology is designed to be a simpler and more affordable alternative to traditional ATP (adenosine triphosphate) testing, reducing false positives from sanitizers and non-hazardous food residues. The swabs are stable at room temperature, simplifying storage and reducing waste. Fresh Check serves clients in the food, hospitality, and healthcare industries, including food manufacturers and food service companies. The business model is centered on selling the consumable swabs and providing access to the digital platform for data capture, trend analysis, and reporting. The company has raised a total of $1.3 million in funding over three rounds and was valued at $2.43 million as of July 2021. Keywords: hygiene verification, contamination detection, food safety, color-chan…', 'https://freshcheck.co.uk', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/fresh-check/', 'https://storage.googleapis.com/dealroom-images-production/2025/09/22/030092d61d983dc3c706858eca77e863.png', 'https://app.dealroom.co/companies/fresh_check', 'London', 'United Kingdom', 51.427357, -0.1305667, 'Life sciences|Hardware|BioTechnology|Food Logistics & Delivery|Testing|Health|Hygiene|B2b Online Marketplace|Hard Tech|EIT Ecosystem|Horizon Europe|medical testing|DT and LS|uk is8 life sciences|science-based|Food', '2015', '8', 3403905, 'life_sciences')
